overage to 90\\% and aligning with \\textbf{Software Defined Lifecycle} security standards.}\n    \\resumeItem{Resolved 20+ critical production incidents using \\textbf{Splunk} and \\textbf{Log4j} for root-cause analysis, improving MTTR by 20\\% in a \\textbf{high-availability SaaS} environment.}\n    \\resumeItem{Built \\textbf{CI/CD pipelines} with \\textbf{GitHub Actions} and \\textbf{SonarQube}, automating builds and security quality gates to reduce deployment cycles by 35\\%.}\n  \\resumeItemListEnd\n\n\\resumeSubheading\n  {Associate Software Engineer}{Jun 2021 -- Jan 2022}\n  {Cognizant Technology Solutions}{Hyderabad, India}\n  \\resumeItemListStart\n    \\resumeItem{Developed backend modules using \\textbf{Java and Spring Boot}, supporting \\textbf{RESTful APIs} and \\textbf{JSON} data processing handling 5K+ daily requests for web-based applications.}\n    \\resumeItem{Configured \\textbf{AWS EC2/RDS} environments for stable software releases, ensuring robust database usage and cloud service reliability.}\n    \\resumeItem{Diagnosed and fixed production defects using \\textbf{Java} and \\textbf{SQL} troubleshooting techniques, reducing repeat software incidents by 20\\% under senior guidance.}\n    \\resumeItem{Maintained 80\\%+ code coverage by developing automated tests with \\textbf{JUnit}, adhering to clean code standards and \\textbf{Agile} development methodologies.}\n  \\resumeItemListEnd\n\n\\resumeSubHeadingListEnd\n\n%-----------PROJECTS-----------\n\\section{Projects}\n\\resumeSubHeadingListStart\n\n\\resumeSubheading\n  {TrackHire AI $|$ \n\\href{https://trackhireai.vercel.app}{\\underline{Live}} $|$ \n\\href{https://github.com/saitejamukkera/Job-Resume-Tracker}{\\underline{GitHub}}}{Jan 2026 -- Present}\n  {\\small Spring Boot, Java, PostgreSQL, Docker, Caddy, OAuth2, LLM Integration}{}\n  \\resumeItemListStart\n    \\resumeItem{Architected a scalable backend with \\textbf{Spring Boot} and \\textbf{Java}, delivering RESTful APIs for job and resume management, user authentication, and notification workflows.}\n    \\resumeItem{Integrated \\textbf{PostgreSQL} for persistent storage, optimizing schema design and leveraging advanced SQL for transactional reliability and performance.}\n    \\resumeItem{Deployed containerized services using \\textbf{Docker Compose} and secured public endpoints with a \\textbf{Caddy} reverse proxy, automating HTTPS and service orchestration.}\n    \\resumeItem{Enabled AI-powered features by integrating a \\textbf{Large Language Model (LLM)} via the Gemini API, supporting intelligent resume analysis and job matching.}\n  \\resumeItemListEnd\n\n\\resumeSubheading\n  {JobRadar (Full-Stack Application) $|$ \\href{https://job-radar.vercel.app}{\\underline{Live}} $|$ \\href{https://github.com/saitejamukkera/job-portal-fullstack-mern}{\\underline{GitHub}}}{Oct 2024 -- Jan 2025}\n  {\\small JavaScript, Node.js, React, MongoDB, Express.js, Redux Toolkit}{}\n  \\resumeItemListStart\n    \\resumeItem{Engineered a scalable Job Board platform using the \\textbf{MERN stack}, implementing \\textbf{RBAC} for Recruiters/Applicants.}\n    \\resumeItem{Developed \\textbf{RESTful APIs} with \\textbf{Express.js} and \\textbf{MongoDB}, enabling advanced filtering and reducing latency by 30\\%.}\n    \\resumeItem{Implemented secure authentication using \\textbf{JWT} and \\textbf{Bcrypt}, managing state with \\textbf{Redux Toolkit}.}\n  \\resumeItemListEnd\n\n\\resumeSubHeadingListEnd\n\n%-----------TECHNICAL SKILLS-----------\n\\section{Technical Skills}\n\\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=0.15in, label={}, itemsep=0.5pt]\n\\small{\\item{\n \\textbf{Programming Languages:} Java, Python, JavaScript, TypeScript, SQL, C++, HTML5, CSS3 \\\\\n \\textbf{Web \\& Frameworks:} React.js, Node.js, Express.js, Spring Boot, RESTful APIs, Redux, TailwindCSS \\\\\n \\textbf{AI/ML \\& Data Science:} TensorFlow, AI/ML Concepts, Data Preprocessing, LLM Integration \\\\\n \\textbf{Cloud \\& Databases:} AWS (EC2, S3, RDS), PostgreSQL, MySQL, MongoDB, Vercel, OAuth2 \\\\\n \\textbf{DevOps \\& Tools:} Docker, Git, GitHub Actions, Splunk, Jira, Confluence, Agile, CI/CD \\\\\n \\textbf{Software Quality:} JUnit, Mockito, SonarQube, Software Testing \\& QA, Linux, Edge Computing\n}}\n\\end{itemize}\n\n\\end{document}\n	Engineer I- Software AI/ML\nApply\nlocations\nAZ - Chandler\ntime type\nFull time\nposted on\nPosted Today\njob requisition id\nR617-26\nAre you looking for a unique opportunity to be a part of something great? Want to join a 17,000-member team that works on the technology that powers the world around us? Looking for an atmosphere of trust, empowerment, respect, diversity, and communication? How about an opportunity to own a piece of a multi-billion dollar (with a B!) global organization? We offer all that and more at Microchip Technology Inc.\n\nPeople come to work at Microchip because we help design the technology that runs the world. They stay because our culture supports their growth and stability. They are challenged and driven by an incredible array of products and solutions with unlimited career potential. Microchip’s nationally-recognized Leadership Passage Programs support career growth where we proudly enroll over a thousand people annually. We take pride in our commitment to employee development, values-based decision making, and strong sense of community, driven by our Vision, Mission, and 11 Guiding Values; we affectionately refer to it as the Aggregate System and it’s won us countless awards for diversity and workplace excellence.\n\nOur company is built by dedicated team players who love to challenge the status quo; we did not achieve record revenue and over 30 years of quarterly profitability without a great team dedicated to empowering innovation. People like you.\n\nVisit our careers page to see what exciting opportunities and company perks await!\n\nJob Description:\n\nWe are seeking a new college graduate to join our Edge AI software engineering team.  The Edge AI software team is responsible for developing software-as-a-service (SAAS) applications for use by our customers to develop AI/ML applications.  You will be collaborating with other software engineers to implement and build our AI/ML toolchain that our customers world-wide use for implementing software AI/ML solutions on Microchip hardware.  You will gain experience in today’s software development techniques, cloud services, hands-on AI/ML workflow experience, AI/ML development toolchain experience, and AI/ML training knowledge while developing world-class software applications that will be used by millions of engineers across the globe. The ideal candidate will have college or university coursework in software engineering with mainstream programming languages, data structures and database usage and web development.  The candidate should have completed software projects using mainstream programming languages, and optionally AI/ML coursework.  Full stack web development and cloud services experience through coursework, software project experience or intern experience is valued.  Candidates that have embedded or IoT experience or used Microchip microcontrollers or microprocessor products in class or coursework is highly valued.\n\nKey Responsibilities:\n\nParticipate in the design, development, and implementation of new and existing software applications using JavaScript, React.js, Python, HTML, MySQL.\n\nDevelop, test and document software application code for our AI/ML applications that will be used by the company and our customers.\n\nCollaborate in an agile development environment with your team members on application requirements and propose innovative solutions.\n\nWork closely with technical leads and other engineers to understand requirements, milestones, and deliverables to build software and SAAS-based products.\n\nUtilize best practices in software development, including code reviews, unit testing, integration, CI/CD and DevOps workflows, Software Defined Lifecycle and software security requirements.\n\nContribute in developing SAAS applications in a cloud-hosted environment.\n\nWrite clean, maintainable, and efficient code, adhering to best practices and coding standards.\n\nDebug, troubleshoot, and resolve software defects and issues.\n\nAssist with the documentation of software solutions, including technical specifications and user guides.\n\nWork with customers and provide support to end-users when necessary.\n\nStay up-to-date with the latest advancements in software development, AI/ML and edge computing technologies to ensure our solutions remain at the cutting edge.\n\nWork in a team environment, developing and fostering a culture of innovation and continuous improvement.\n\nRequirements/Qualifications:\n\nBachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering or related field.\n\nCollege coursework and 0-3 years of experience on software development and software project experience using an Agile software development lifecycle workflow.\n\nStrong understanding of object-oriented programming principles and design patterns.\n\nFamiliarity with SQL and database design concepts.\n\nCoursework in programming languages Java, C, C++, C#, Python, JavaScript or JavaScript-based frameworks such as  React.js, Angular.js, or Vue.js. \n\nCoursework or project experience with web development using languages and technologies such as Python, PHP, Angular.js, React.js, JavaScript, HTML, CSS, JSON, XML/YAML and OAuth API communication methods.\n\nExcellent communication, interpersonal skills, problem-solving skills and the ability to work independently and as part of a team.\n\nEagerness to learn, adapt, and take on new challenges.\n\nPreferred Qualifications:\n\nMaster’s degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering or related field.\n\nKnowledge in using machine learning development tools and frameworks, such as the MPLAB Machine Learning Development Suite and Python AI/ML libraries using TensorFlow/TFLite, Pytorch, Keras, and ONNX.\n\nFamiliarity with cloud computing platforms (AWS, Azure, GCP, OCI) and edge-to-cloud integration.\n\nUse of Agentic AI in software development and MCP server development.\n\nKnowledge of Jira, Confluence, Github/Gitlab/Bitbucket tools.\n\nKnowledge of data collection, preprocessing, and training neural networks in data centers.\n\nSolid understanding of edge computing architectures, including IoT devices, embedded systems, and real-time processing.\n\nKnowledge of IoT embedded computing and software/firmware development on hardware.\n\nExperience with edge computing platforms and optimizing AI/ML models for resource-constrained devices.\n\nTravel Time:\n\n0% - 25%\nPhysical Attributes:\n\nHearing, Seeing, Talking, Works Alone, Works Around Others\nPhysical Requirements:\n\n80% sitting, 10% standing, 10% walking, 100% inside.\nPay Range:\n\nWe offer a total compensation package that ranks among the best in the industry. It consists of competitive base pay, restricted stock units, and quarterly bonus payments. In addition to these components, our package includes health benefits that begin day one, retirement savings plans, and an industry leading ESPP program with a 2 year look back feature. Find more information about all our benefits at the link below:\nBenefits of working at Microchip\n\nThe annual base salary range for this position, which could be performed in the US, is $70,304-$143,000.*\n*Range is dependent on numerous factors including job location, skills and experience.\n\nMicrochip Technology Inc is an equal opportunity/affirmative action employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to sex, gender identity, sexual orientation, race, color, religion, national origin, disability, protected Veteran status, age, or any other characteristic protected by law.\n	R617-26	Chandler, AZ	ACTIVE	Engineer I- Software AI/ML	7
