cial services firm providing investment banking, securities, and investment management services to a substantial and diversified client base that includes corporations, financial institutions, governments, and individuals.\n\nAbout the Global Currency and Emerging Markets Business (GCEM): Our business plays a critical role for the firm in assisting our clients in managing their financial risk in the global currency market as well as local emerging markets. These markets are very sensitive to global events, which leads to an incredibly dynamic and interesting set of business activities and projects.  GCEM is a key source of revenue for the Global Banking and Markets division, and for the firm in general.\n\n \n\nYour Role and Responsibilities: As a developer in this team, you will have the opportunity to:\n\nDevelop software that \nEnable our clients to transact electronically to increase the scale of our business.\nLeverage GS AI tools to create insights and trend analysis for our salespeople and traders to find new opportunities.\nAssist traders in managing their financial risk in real time.\nEnable our business to create and trade new financial products.\nCollaborate with business users, operational teams, and other engineering teams to develop innovative solutions and will be responsible for building and maintaining reliable and scalable systems.\nParticipate in the entire software development life cycle from gathering requirements, designing technical solutions, software implementation, testing, production release through to post-migration support.\nWork both independently and collaboratively within teams, demonstrating the ability to deliver individually, while also supporting group initiatives to achieve shared goals.\n \n\nWhat We Offer:\n\nGlobal Exposure: Work with international teams and gain insights into different markets.\nInnovative Projects: Engage in projects that leverage the latest technologies and methodologies.\nProfessional Growth: Continuous learning opportunities and career development programs.\nCollaborative Environment: Work in a team-oriented environment that values diverse perspectives and ideas.\n \n\nWhat We Are Looking For:\n\nStrong analytical skills and a passion for problem solving.\nStrong programming skills in OO languages such as Java or Python.\nAbility to quickly learn new languages and technologies.\nStrong background in computer science, mathematics, and/or a related field.\nComfort with multi-tasking and is self-motivated.\nInterest in learning about the financial industry.\nExcellent written and verbal communication skills.\nSalary Range\nThe expected base salary for this New York, New York, United States-based position is $115000-$180000. In addition, you may be eligible for a discretionary bonus if you are an active employee as of fiscal year-end.\n\nBenefits\nGoldman Sachs is committed to providing our people with valuable and competitive benefits and wellness offerings, as it is a core part of providing a strong overall employee experience. A summary of these offerings, which are generally available to active, non-temporary, full-time and part-time US employees who work at least 20 hours per week, can be found here.\n\n		New York, NY	ACTIVE	Global Currency and Emerging Markets (GCEM) - Software Engineer	7
