ctions} and \\textbf{Jenkins}, ensuring seamless delivery of features to \\textbf{AWS} environments such as \\textbf{EC2, SNS, S3}.}\n  \\resumeItemListEnd\n\n\\resumeSubheading\n  {Associate Software Engineer}{Aug 2021 -- Oct 2022}\n  {Cognizant Technology Solutions}{Hyderabad, India}\n  \\resumeItemListStart\n    \\resumeItem{Developed backend modules using \\textbf{Java} and \\textbf{SpringBoot}, collaborating with cross-functional teams to deliver stable features for internal incentive systems.}\n    \\resumeItem{Translated \\textbf{Figma} designs into reusable \\textbf{React.js} components and optimized \\textbf{SQL} queries in \\textbf{PostgreSQL} to support data-intensive financial dashboards.}\n    \\resumeItem{Performed rigorous functional testing and code reviews using \\textbf{Git}, ensuring all software releases adhered to enterprise security and performance standards.}\n  \\resumeItemListEnd\n\n\\resumeSubHeadingListEnd\n\n%-----------PROJECTS-----------\n\\section{Projects}\n\\resumeSubHeadingListStart\n\n\\resumeSubheading\n  {TrackHire AI $|$ \n\\href{https://trackhireai.vercel.app}{\\underline{Live}} $|$ \n\\href{https://github.com/saitejamukkera/Job-Resume-Tracker}{\\underline{GitHub}}}{Jan 2026 -- Present}\n  {\\small Spring Boot, Java, PostgreSQL, Docker, Caddy, OAuth2, LLM Integration}{}\n  \\resumeItemListStart\n    \\resumeItem{Architected a scalable backend with \\textbf{Spring Boot} and \\textbf{Java}, delivering RESTful APIs for job and resume management, user authentication, and notification workflows.}\n    \\resumeItem{Integrated \\textbf{PostgreSQL} for persistent storage, optimizing schema design and leveraging advanced SQL for transactional reliability and performance.}\n    \\resumeItem{Deployed containerized services using \\textbf{Docker Compose} and secured public endpoints with a \\textbf{Caddy} reverse proxy, automating HTTPS and service orchestration.}\n    \\resumeItem{Enabled AI-powered features by integrating a \\textbf{Large Language Model (LLM)} via the Gemini API, supporting intelligent resume analysis and job matching.}\n  \\resumeItemListEnd\n\n\\resumeSubheading\n  {JobRadar (Full-Stack Application) $|$ \\href{https://job-radar.vercel.app}{\\underline{Live}} $|$ \\href{https://github.com/saitejamukkera/job-portal-fullstack-mern}{\\underline{GitHub}}}{Oct 2024 -- Jan 2025}\n  {\\small JavaScript, Node.js, React, MongoDB, Express.js, Redux Toolkit}{}\n  \\resumeItemListStart\n    \\resumeItem{Engineered a scalable Job Board platform using the \\textbf{MERN stack}, implementing \\textbf{RBAC} for Recruiters/Applicants.}\n    \\resumeItem{Developed \\textbf{RESTful APIs} with \\textbf{Express.js} and \\textbf{MongoDB}, enabling advanced filtering and reducing latency by 30\\%.}\n    \\resumeItem{Implemented secure authentication using \\textbf{JWT} and \\textbf{Bcrypt}, managing state with \\textbf{Redux Toolkit}.}\n  \\resumeItemListEnd\n\n\\resumeSubHeadingListEnd\n\n%-----------TECHNICAL SKILLS-----------\n\\section{Technical Skills}\n\\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=0.15in, label={}, itemsep=2pt]\n\\small{\\item{\n \\textbf{Programming Languages}{: Java, JavaScript (ES6+), TypeScript, SQL, Python} \\\\\n \\textbf{Backend Technologies}{: Spring Boot, Node.js, Express.js, RESTful APIs, Microservices} \\\\\n \\textbf{Frontend Technologies}{: React.js, Redux Toolkit, HTML5, CSS3 (Flexbox/Grid), TailwindCSS} \\\\\n \\textbf{Databases \\& Cloud}{: PostgreSQL, MongoDB, MySQL, Oracle, AWS (EC2, S3, RDS), GCP} \\\\\n \\textbf{DevOps \\& Tools}{: Git, Jenkins, GitHub Actions, Docker, Splunk, SonarQube, Figma, Agile} \\\\\n \\textbf{IDEs}{: IntelliJ IDEA, VS Code, Eclipse, Cursor}\n}}\n\\end{itemize}\n\n\\end{document}	Software Engineer\nApply\nlocations\nUSA Remote\ntime type\nFull time\nposted on\nPosted Today\njob requisition id\nR4193\nJoin us in creating a better way!\nAt eHealth, our mission is to expertly guide consumers through their health insurance and related options when, where, and how they prefer. We’re creating a better way – one that’s transparent and trustworthy for both our consumers externally and our employees internally. \n\nMove your career forward while connecting countless people to the life- changing, quality care they deserve. Our diverse team of innovators supports one another in solving some of the toughest challenges. We’re always on the lookout for creative opportunities to do right by our customers, and each other. Together, we’re creating a better way to work, united by our common passion to make a difference.\n\nAt eHealth, our mission is to expertly guide our customers through their health insurance needs, providing personalized and affordable plans. Through our proprietary marketplace, we offer quality Medicare insurance options which includes Medicare Advantage, Supplement, and Prescription Drug, Individual, Family, Small Business, and Ancillary from 200 carriers nationwide. Our vision is to be the nation's leading source for health insurance and related products.\nWe are seeking a Software Engineer to join the Financial Systems team. In this role, you will spearhead the architecture, design, and development of our critical in-house software systems, which are responsible for core business functions such as revenue recognition and incentive compensation. These applications are used directly by our Finance and Revenue Operations teams. Collaborating closely with cross-functional teams, you'll establish best practices for full-stack software development, ensuring the reliability, performance, and scalability of these essential financial applications. Your contributions will span the entire lifecycle of these internal systems, driving our mission to deliver accurate, efficient, and high-quality financial technology experiences at scale.\nHow you will make an impact:\nYou have proven industry experience in software design and development. You are a solutioncentric, results-oriented, and experienced Software Engineer. You want to “build what’s right, not what’s easy.” You will work with other engineers in a collaborative environment to improve the overall quality while achieving timely delivery of solutions. You are ambitious, talented, and driven to make the team and project successful.\nWhat you'll do:\nHands-on implementation of in-house software systems for core financial functions, including revenue recognition and incentive compensation.\nCollaborate closely with cross-functional engineers and stakeholders from Finance and Revenue Operations to deliver high-quality solutions, including robust unit, integration, and functional tests and code reviews.\nEngage with leaders and team members across Engineering and Finance to provide valuable insights on technically feasible solutions for financial processes.\nContribute to the software engineering standards and evaluate technology options to ensure the optimal performance, reliability, and scalability of critical financial applications.\nThrive in a dynamic environment characterized by rapid iterations, continuous learning, and a passion for overcoming obstacles.\nWho you are:\n\nYou have a BS in Computer Science or similar field\nYou bring 2+ years of hands-on experience in fast-paced full-stack product development environments.\nYou have experience with backend service design, development and testing using NodeJS and/or Java SpringBoot\nYou have experience with one of modern Javascript front-end development technologies like Vue.js, React.js, Next.js, and Nuxt.js, emphasizing reusable component design and mobile-friendly user interfaces with CSS techniques such as grids, flexbox, and breakpoints and standards such as ES6, ES5 .\nYou have experience working with Product Managers and UX designers to understand the requirements and translate the FIGMA UI designs into implementations.\nYou have experience in working with SQL and NoSQL databases (e.g., Oracle, Postgres, MongoDB).\nYou have an understanding of microservices architecture, RESTful services and cloud-native software development.\nYou have experience in working with GIT, Jenkins, AWS/GCP, CI/CD.\nYou have experience in working with feature flagging, A/B testing (Adobe, Target, Optimizely), distributed tracing, Server Side Rendering, Performance improvement and testing for full-stack eCommerce application is a plus. Knowledge of web page performance optimization and relevant metrics is a plus.\nWhat we offer:\n\nGenerous benefits include medical, dental and vision beginning on your first day of employment\n401K with matching\nTuition reimbursement\nEmployee stock purchase program\n12 company paid holidays and flexible time off (PTO for non-exempt)\nOur Values: At eHealth, our core values guide our work:\n\nOne Team\nCustomer Centric\nInnovation\nIntegrity\nQuality\nAccountability\nRelentless \nFinancial Stewardship\n*Please note the above is a summary of responsibilities; a full job description is available upon request. \n\nJob Application Deadline: February 24, 2026\n\n#LI-Remote\n\n#LI- DC\n\n-\n\nThe base pay range reflects the anticipated pay range for this position. The actual base pay offered will depend on various factors including individual skills, experience, performance, qualifications, the department budget, and the location where work is performed. Base pay is one component of eHealth’s total rewards package, which also includes an annual performance bonus, plus an array of benefits designed to support employees’ personal and professional wellness. For more information on our total rewards offerings, please visit our career site.\n-\n\nBase Pay Range -$104,600 - $130,700\n-\n\neHealth is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer. It is our policy to provide equal opportunity to all employees and applicants and to prohibit any discrimination because of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, marital status, sexual orientation, genetic information, disability, protected veteran status, or any other consideration made unlawful by applicable federal, state or local laws. The foundation of these policies is our commitment to treat everyone fairly and equally and to have a bias-free work environment.\n\n	R4193	USA Remote	ACTIVE	Software Engineer	7
