nt pipelines using GitHub Actions to ensure consistent, error-free releases. Additionally, I am comfortable with full-stack integration, having utilized React to build internal monitoring dashboards that interface with complex backend systems. Whether optimizing SQL queries for transactional reliability or integrating LLMs for intelligent data analysis, I focus on creating maintainable code that addresses real-world challenges in high-concurrency environments.\n\nDuring my Master's program, I studied Software Testing and Quality Assurance as well as Advanced Algorithms, which allows me to contribute to Tesla by ensuring that every line of code is optimized for performance and validated against the highest standards of reliability. My academic focus on Advanced Computer Networking and Security also provides me with the necessary perspective to build secure backend systems that can withstand the demands of a global manufacturing network. I have also developed a foundational understanding of AI tools, which I am keen to leverage to improve factory automation and predictive monitoring.\n\nI am deeply inspired by Tesla's culture of rapid innovation and technical excellence. I am confident that my backend expertise, coupled with my proactive problem-solving mindset and passion for factory software, will allow me to make a significant impact on your team. I look forward to the possibility of discussing how my experience in building resilient, scalable systems can support the next generation of Tesla products.\n\nThank you for your time and consideration. I look forward to the possibility of discussing how I can contribute to the Factory Software team.\n\nSincerely,\nSai Teja Mukkera\nhttps://www.saitejamukkera.dev\nhttps://www.github.com/saitejamukkera	\\documentclass[letterpaper,10pt]{article}\n\n\\usepackage{latexsym}\n\\usepackage[empty]{fullpage}\n\\usepackage{titlesec}\n\\usepackage[usenames,dvipsnames]{color}\n\\usepackage{enumitem}\n\\usepackage[hidelinks]{hyperref}