 applying AI- and agentic-driven capabilities to help travelers resolve their needs intuitively. My experience with Docker and CI/CD pipelines enables me to contribute to the team’s goal of delivering incremental, shippable deliverables while adhering to strict code quality and observability standards.\n\nDuring my Master's program, I studied Software Testing & Quality Assurance, which allows me to implement advanced testing methodologies and ensure the reliability of distributed systems. My coursework in Introduction to Cloud Computing further prepared me to design and operate services that are both scalable and fungible across different domains. I am a strong advocate for Clean Code practices and thrive in Agile environments where collaboration across Product, Design, and Engineering is essential to success.\n\nI have long admired Expedia’s commitment to fostering a diverse and inclusive culture that puts people first. I am confident that my blend of backend expertise, full-stack curiosity, and dedication to high-quality engineering will enable me to make immediate contributions to the Servicing team. Thank you for your time and consideration. I look forward to the possibility of discussing how I can contribute to building the future of travel with Expedia Group.\n\nSincerely,\nSai Teja Mukkera\nhttps://www.saitejamukkera.dev\nhttps://www.github.com/saitejamukkera	%-------------------------\n% Resume in Latex (ATS Optimized) - 1 Page Jobright Style + Icons\n%------------------------\n\n\\documentclass[letterpaper,10pt]{article}\n\n\\usepackage{latexsym}\n\\usepackage[empty]{fullpage}\n\\usepackage{titlesec}\n\\usepackage{marvosym}\n\\usepackage[usenames,dvipsnames]{color}\n\\usepackage{enumitem}\n\\usepackage[hidelinks]{hyperref}\n\\usepackage{fancyhdr}\n\\usepackage{fontawesome5}\n\\usepackage[english]{babel}\n\\usepackage{tabularx}\n\\input{glyphtounicode}\n\n\\pagestyle{fancy}\n\\fancyhf{}\n\\fancyfoot{}\n\\renewcommand{\\headrulewidth}{0pt}\n\\renewcommand{\\f