uilding scalable, traveler-centric self-service solutions using \\textbf{Java, Spring Boot, and Node.js}. Proven track record in designing \\textbf{high-availability REST APIs} and \\textbf{React-based UIs}, with a focus on \\textbf{operational excellence} and \\textbf{clean code} principles. Eager to contribute to Expedia Group’s Servicing team by integrating \\textbf{AI-driven capabilities} and optimizing full-stack experiences to drive traveler satisfaction and platform reliability.\n\n%-----------EDUCATION-----------\n\\section{Education}\n\\resumeSubHeadingListStart\n  \\resumeSubheading\n    {University of Central Missouri}{Warrensburg, MO, USA}\n    {Master of Science in Computer Science \\textbf{(GPA: 4.0)}}{Jan 2024 -- Dec 2025}\n  \\resumeSubheading\n    {Guru Nanak Institute of Technology}{Hyderabad, India}\n    {Bachelor of Technology in Electronics and Communication Engineering}{Jul 2015 -- Jul 2019}\n\\resumeSubHeadingListEnd\n\n%-----------EXPERIENCE-----------\n\\section{Experience}\n\\resumeSubHeadingListStart\n\n\\resumeSubheading\n  {Software Engineer}{Nov 2022 -- Dec 2023}\n  {Cognizant Technology Solutions}{Hyderabad, India}\n  \\resumeItemListStart\n    \\resumeItem{Engineered scalable microservices using \\textbf{Java, Spring Boot and Node.js}, delivering high-concurrency self-service modules for enterprise clients that improved system reliability for over 10k daily users.}\n    \\resumeItem{Refactored \\textbf{RESTful API} request/response structures using \\textbf{DTOs} and \\textbf{Lombok}, reducing payload latency by \\textbf{40\\%} and optimizing data modeling for \\textbf{Node.js and React} frontend consumption.}\n    \\resumeItem{Implemented rigorous \\textbf{Input Validation (JSR-303)} and \\textbf{Clean Code} patterns in the service layer, securing data integrity and reducing production logic errors by \\textbf{15\\%}.}\n    \\resumeItem{Authored comprehensive automated test suites using \\textbf{JUnit 5 and Mockito}, maintaining \\textbf{90\\% code coverage} to support incremental, shippable deliverables in an Agile environment.}\n    \\resumeItem{Spearheaded production incident resolution using \\textbf{Splunk and Log4j} observability tools, diagnosing root causes for 40+ defects to maintain 99.9\\% uptime for critical servicing features.}\n    \\resumeItem{Collaborated in CI/CD automation via \\textbf{GitHub Actions} and \\textbf{SonarQube}, enforcing quality gates to ensure performant, secure, and maintainable software components for distributed teams.}\n  \\resumeItemListEnd\n\n\\resumeSubheading\n  {Associate Software Engineer}{Aug 2021 -- Oct 2022}\n  {Cognizant Technology Solutions}{Hyderabad, India}\n  \\resumeItemListStart\n    \\resumeItem{Contributed to backend feature development using \\textbf{Java and Spring Boot}, implementing modular service logic and data persistence strategies to support traveler-facing applications.}\n    \\resumeItem{Maintained and debugged \\textbf{RESTful APIs} and \\textbf{SQL} data stores, resolving integration bugs and improving the responsiveness of traveler self-service workflows.}\n    \\resumeItem{Validated software components through structured unit testing with \\textbf{JUnit}, ensuring high-quality code delivery and alignment with enterprise architectural standards.}\n  \\resumeItemListEnd\n\n\\resumeSubHeadingListEnd\n\n%-----------PROJECTS-----------\n\\section{Projects}\n\\resumeSubHeadingListStart\n\n\\resumeSubheading\n  {TrackHire AI $|$ \\hspace{1pt}\n\\href{https://trackhireai.vercel.app}{\\faLink} \\hspace{2pt} \n\\href{https://github.com/saitejamukkera/Job-Resume-Tracker}{\\faGithub}}{Jan 2026 -- Present}\n  {\\small Spring Boot, Java, PostgreSQL, Docker, Caddy, OAuth2, LLM Integration}{}\n  \\resumeItemListStart\n    \\resumeItem{Architected a scalable backend with \\textbf{Spring Boot} and \\textbf{Java}, delivering RESTful APIs for job and resume management, user authentication, and notification workflows.}\n    \\resumeItem{Integrated \\textbf{PostgreSQL} for persistent storage, optimizing schema design and leveraging advanced SQL for transactional reliability and performance.}\n    \\resumeItem{Deployed containerized services using \\textbf{Docker Compose} and secured public endpoints with a \\textbf{Caddy} reverse proxy, automating HTTPS and service orchestration.}\n    \\resumeItem{Enabled AI-powered features by integrating a \\textbf{Large Language Model (LLM)} via the Gemini API, supporting intelligent resume analysis and job matching.}\n  \\resumeItemListEnd\n\n\\resumeSubheading\n  {JobRadar (Full-Stack Application) $|$ \\hspace{1pt} \\href{https://job-radar.vercel.app}{\\faLink} \\hspace{2pt} \\href{https://github.com/saitejamukkera/job-portal-fullstack-mern}{\\faGithub}}{Oct 2024 -- Jan 2025}\n  {JavaScript, Node.js, React, MongoDB, Express.js, Redux Toolkit}{}\n  \\resumeItemListStart\n    \\resumeItem{Engineered a scalable Job Board platform using the \\textbf{MERN stack}, implementing \\textbf{RBAC} for Recruiters/Applicants.}\n    \\resumeItem{Developed \\textbf{RESTful APIs} with \\textbf{Express.js} and \\textbf{MongoDB}, enabling advanced filtering and reducing latency by 30\\%.}\n    \\resumeItem{Implemented secure authentication using \\textbf{JWT} and \\textbf{Bcrypt}, managing state with \\textbf{Redux Toolkit}.}\n  \\resumeItemListEnd\n\n\\resumeSubHeadingListEnd\n\n%-----------TECHNICAL SKILLS-----------\n\\section{Technical Skills}\n\\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=0.15in, label={}, itemsep=2pt]\n\\small{\\item{\n \\textbf{Programming Languages}{: Java, JavaScript, TypeScript, SQL, Python} \\\\\n \\textbf{Backend Technologies}{: Spring Boot, Node.js, Express.js, RESTful APIs} \\\\\n \\textbf{Frontend Technologies}{: React, Redux, HTML5, CSS3, Bootstrap, TailwindCSS} \\\\\n \\textbf{Databases \\& Cloud}{: PostgreSQL, MongoDB, MySQL, AWS (EC2, S3, RDS), Vercel} \\\\\n \\textbf{DevOps, AI \\& Tools}{: Docker, Git, GitHub Actions, Jenkins, Splunk, AI/ML Integration, Agile} \\\\\n \\textbf{IDEs}{: IntelliJ IDEA, VS Code, Cursor, Claude Code, Eclipse}\n}}\n\\end{itemize}\n\n\\end{document}	Software Development Engineer II\nExpedia Group brands power global travel for everyone, everywhere. We design cutting-edge tech to make travel smoother and more memorable, and we create groundbreaking solutions for our partners. Our diverse, vibrant, and welcoming community is essential in driving our success.\n\nWhy Join Us?\n\nTo shape the future of travel, people must come first. Guided by our Values and Leadership Agreements, we foster an open culture where everyone belongs, differences are celebrated and know that when one of us wins, we all win.\n\nWe provide a full benefits package, including exciting travel perks, generous time-off, parental leave, a flexible work model (with some pretty cool offices), and career development resources, all to fuel our employees' passion for travel and ensure a rewarding career journey. We’re building a more open world. Join us.\n\nOur Technology Team partners with teams across Expedia Group to create innovative products, services, and tools to deliver high-quality experiences for travelers, partners, and our employees. A singular technology platform powered by data and machine learning provides secure, differentiated, and personalized experiences that drive loyalty and traveler satisfaction.\n\nIntroduction to the Team\n\nExpedia Technology teams partner with our Product teams to create innovative products, services, and tools to deliver high-quality experiences for travelers, partners, and our employees. A singular technology platform powered by data and machine learning provides secure, differentiated, and personalized experiences that drive loyalty and traveler satisfaction.\n\nThe Software Development Engineer II position is part of the Servicing team, which builds and supports Web and Native App traveler self-service experiences for all Expedia brands and partners. In this role, you will design, build, and operate servicing experiences across web and native apps, collaborating closely with Product, XD, and Program Management.\n\nYou will contribute to the technical design and implementation of scalable services and user experiences in the traveler Servicing space, including applying AI- and agentic-driven capabilities to help travelers resolve their needs quickly and intuitively. As an SDE II, you will be a hands-on engineer, owning features end-to-end and helping to elevate engineering practices on the team through high-quality code, testing, and operational excellence.\n\nIn this role, you will:\n\nDesign, develop, test, and maintain high-quality software components and services, contributing to low-level system design, API design, and data modeling within your team’s domain.\n\nImplement robust, secure, and performant code using established engineering best practices, including automated testing, code reviews, observability, and continuous integration and delivery.\n\nCollaborate with product, design, and engineering peers to refine requirements into clear technical solutions, breaking down work into incremental, shippable deliverables.\n\nTroubleshoot, debug, and resolve production issues, improving reliability, scalability, and operational excellence of services you own or support.\n\nSafely integrate and operate AI/ML‑enabled solutions that improve outcomes, including familiarity with AI-driven systems, tools, or workflows and applying AI/ML concepts to real world products.\n\nContribute to documentation, knowledge sharing, and cross-team collaboration, enabling your solutions to be reusable and fungible across multiple services and domains.\n\nMinimum Qualifications:\n\nBachelor’s degree in Computer Science or a related technical field; or Equivalent related professional experience.\n\n2+ years of relevant professional experience.\n\nProfessional software development experience working on production systems and services.\n\nExperience owning and delivering components or services within a larger system, including responsibility for design, implementation, testing, and operational readiness.\n\nProficiency in at least one modern programming language and core computer science fundamentals such as data structures, algorithms, object-oriented design, and distributed systems basics, including experience building and consuming APIs and working with relational or NoSQL data stores.\n\nPreferred Qualifications:\n\n2+ years of full‑stack development experience across front‑end and back‑end services\n\nRecent hands-on experience building and operating Node.js + React-based applications in production\n\nExperience implementing and maintaining GraphQL-based backends\n\nExperience designing and implementing service APIs and data models consumed by multiple teams or products\n\nExperience running production services with monitoring, alerting, and on-call participation (e.g., pager rotation)\n\nExperience as a Clean Code practitioner committed to producing high-quality code.\n\nSolid experience with agile project methodologies and working with distributed teams.\n\nPlease note that this role is only available in Austin in alignment with our flexible work model which requires employees to be in-office at least three days a week. We are unable to offer relocation assistance for this role.\n\nThe total cash range for this position in Austin is $119,000.00 to $166,500.00. Employees in this role have the potential to increase their pay up to $190,500.00, which is the top of the range, based on ongoing, demonstrated, and sustained performance in the role.\nStarting pay for this role will vary based on multiple factors, including location, available budget, and an individual’s knowledge, skills, and experience. Pay ranges may be modified in the future.\n\nExpedia Group is proud to offer a wide range of benefits to support employees and their families, including medical/dental/vision, paid time off, and an Employee Assistance Program. To fuel each employee’s passion for travel, we offer a wellness & travel reimbursement, travel discounts, and an International Airlines Travel Agent (IATAN) membership. View our full list of benefits.\n\n		Warrensburg, MO	ACTIVE	Software Development Engineer II	7
27	2026-02-14 00:34:10.85262	Microsoft	Sai Teja Mukkera\nWarrensburg, MO\n9139639317\nsaitejamukkera@gmail.com\nhttps://www.linkedin.com/in/saiteja-mukkera\n\nFebruary 14, 2026\nHiring Manager\nMicrosoft\nOne Microsoft Way, Redmond, WA 98052\n\nRe: Application for Software Engineer (Job ID: 200023528)\n\nDear Hiring Manager,\nI am writing to express my strong interest in the Software Engineer position for the Azure Resource Builder (ARB) team at Microsoft. As a Software Engineer with over two years of professional experience and a Master of Science in Computer Science with a 4.0 GPA, I have developed a deep fascination for building high-performance, massively distributed cloud software. My background in Java-based backend engineering, combined with my academic focus on distributed systems and cloud architecture, aligns perfectly with ARB’s mission to provide a powerful processing pipeline for Azure’s global inventory.\n\nDuring my tenure at Cognizant, I specialized in engineering scalable microservices using Java and Spring Boot. I successfully refactored API structures using DTO patterns, which reduced JSON payload sizes by 40% and significantly improved network throughput for distributed clients. I also took ownership of live-site maintenance using Splunk and Log4j, where I resolved over 40 critical production defects, ensuring the high availability and operational stability that a service like ARB demands. These experiences taught me how to write exemplary, maintainable code that can withstand the pressures of a fast-paced production environment.\n\nMy technical contributions extended to building robust automated test suites with JUnit 5 and Mockito, where I achieved 90% code coverage and reduced regression defects by 25%. This focus on quality and simplicity is a core tenet I bring to every project. Furthermore, I have hands-on experience in full-stack delivery, including optimizing frontend performance for complex applications, which allows me to understand end-to-end user scenarios—from the Azure Portal interface down to the underlying data processing engine.\n\nDuring my Master's program, I studied Introduction to Cloud Computing and Advanced Algorithms, which allows me to approach large-scale data processing challenges with a strong theoretical foundation in scalability and efficiency. My proficiency in Java, combined with my exposure to AWS and fundamental understanding of Azure services, enables me to contribute immediately to the ARB vision of processing billions of cloud resources. I am also familiar with Docker and CI/CD automation through GitHub Actions, ensuring that I can integrate seamlessly into Microsoft’s agile engineering culture.\n\nI am particularly excited about the ARB team because of the opportunity to solve prominent problems for large enterprise customers using cutting-edge technologies. Microsoft’s culture of a growth mindset and innovation resonates with my own commitment to continuous learning and technical excellence. I am confident that my experience in building resilient backend systems and my drive to design at scale make me an excellent fit for your team.\n\nThank you for your time and consideration. I look forward to the possibility of discussing how I can contribute to the performance and scalability goals of the Azure Resource Builder team.\n\nSincerely,\nSai Teja Mukkera\nhttps://saiteja-dev-portfolio.vercel.app\nhttps://www.github.com/saitejamukkera	%-------------------------\n% Resume in Latex (ATS Optimized) - 1 Page Jobright Style (Text Only)\n%------------------------\n\n\\documentclass[letterpaper,10pt]{article}\n\n\\usepackage{latexsym}\n\\usepackage[empty]{fullpage}\n\\usepackage{titlesec}\n\\usepackage[usenames,dvipsnames]{color}\n\\usepackage{enumitem}\n\\usepackage[hidelinks]{hyperref}\n\\usepackage{fancyhdr}\n\\usepackage[english]{babel}\n\\usepackage{tabularx}\n\\input{glyphtounicode}\n\n\\pagestyle{fancy}\n\\fancyhf{}\n\\fancyfoot{}\n\\renewcommand{\\headrulewidth}{0pt}\n\\