use score} across metrics.}\n  \\resumeItemListEnd\n\n\\resumeSubheading\n  {JobRadar (Full-Stack Application) $|$ \\href{https://job-radar.vercel.app}{\\underline{Live}} $|$ \\href{https://github.com/saitejamukkera/job-portal-fullstack-mern}{\\underline{GitHub}}}{Oct 2024 -- Jan 2025}\n  {\\small JavaScript, Node.js, React, MongoDB, Express.js, Redux Toolkit}{}\n  \\resumeItemListStart\n    \\resumeItem{Engineered a scalable Job Board platform using the \\textbf{MERN stack}, implementing \\textbf{RBAC} for Recruiters/Applicants.}\n    \\resumeItem{Developed \\textbf{RESTful APIs} with \\textbf{Express.js} and \\textbf{MongoDB}, enabling advanced filtering and reducing latency by 30\\%}\n    \\resumeItem{Implemented secure authentication using \\textbf{JWT} and \\textbf{Bcrypt}, managing state with \\textbf{Redux Toolkit}.}\n  \\resumeItemListEnd\n\n\\resumeSubHeadingListEnd\n\n%-----------TECHNICAL SKILLS-----------\n\\section{Technical Skills}\n\\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=0.15in, label={}, itemsep=2pt]\n\\small{\\item{\n \\textbf{Programming Languages}{: Java, C\\# (Knowledgeable), JavaScript, TypeScript, SQL, Python} \\\\\n \\textbf{Backend Technologies}{: Spring Boot, Distributed Systems, RESTful APIs, Node.js, Express.js} \\\\\n \\textbf{Frontend Technologies}{: React, Redux, HTML5, CSS3, Bootstrap, TailwindCSS} \\\\\n \\textbf{Databases \\& Cloud}{: PostgreSQL, MongoDB, MySQL, Azure/AWS Fundamentals (EC2, S3, RDS), Vercel} \\\\\n \\textbf{DevOps, AI \\& Tools}{: Docker, Git, GitHub Actions, Jenkins, Splunk, AI/ML Concepts, Agile} \\\\\n \\textbf{IDEs}{: IntelliJ IDEA, Eclipse, Cursor, VS Code, Claude Code}\n}}\n\\end{itemize}\n\n\\end{document}	Software Engineer\nUnited States, Multiple Locations, Multiple Locations\nApply now\n\nAdd to cart\n\n\nFind out how well you match with this job\n\nUpload your resume\n\nJob description\n\nCompany and benefits\nJob number\n200023528\nDate posted\nFeb 12, 2026\nWork site\n0 days / week in-office – remote\nTravel\nLess than 25%\nProfession\nSoftware Engineering\nDiscipline\nSoftware Engineering\nRole type\nIndividual Contributor\nEmployment type\nFull-Time\nOverview\nAzure Resource Builder (ARB) is a data processing engine which fuels Azure Resource Graph (ARG) and overall, One Inventory of cloud and other Microsoft resources and is a core service enabling @scale experiences like ARG, Azure Portal, Azure Search, Azure Change. It provides a powerful processing pipeline within the Azure Control Plane providing processing capabilities closer to where the inventory data exists. ARB’s vision is to enable any customer (first party or third party) to build inventory data-based solutions with little effort and enable these values to all of Azure customers. So naturally, scale and performance are our team’s DNA. Anything we design, develop, or deliver aligns with this vision.\n\nWe are the Azure Resource Builder team processing billions of cloud resources. Our mission is to be the best self-managing, high performing, and highly available platform. Our environment is fast-paced and highly innovative. As a member of team, you will have the opportunity to work with top-notch engineers and domain experts to help develop Azure-wide data processing engine to support real-time scenarios across billions of resources. You will be immersed in many exciting, cutting-edge technologies with immense opportunity for growth and immediate business impact.\n\nOur team innovates quickly and works closely with partners and customers in an agile, high-energy environment. If the opportunity to collaborate with diverse engineering teams on enabling end-to-end auditing, change insights and diagnosability scenarios using cutting-edge technologies and solving prominent problems for large enterprise customers excites you, please come and talk to us!\n\nMicrosoft’s mission is to empower every person and every organization on the planet to achieve more. As employees we come together with a growth mindset, innovate to empower others and collaborate to realize our shared goals. Each day we build on our values of respect, integrity, and accountability to create a culture of inclusion where everyone can thrive at work and beyond.\n\n\n\nResponsibilities\nPlans, designs, develops, and tests software systems used in massively distributed cloud-based software.\nDevelops software, tools, and code to be used in support of design, infrastructure, and technology platforms as well as commercial or end-user applications.\nWrites exemplary code working with large scale distributed systems with quality, simplicity, and maintainability as core tenets.\nCommunicates effectively and partners with other disciplines of the project team to deliver high quality solutions from ideas to production code.\nContributes to live site maintenance activities. \n\n\nQualifications\nRequired Qualifications:\n\nBachelor's Degree in Computer Science, or related technical discipline with proven experience coding in languages including, but not limited to, Java, C++, C# or object-oriented programming\nOR equivalent experience.\nOther Requirements:\n\nAbility to meet Microsoft, customer and/or government security screening requirements are required for this role. These requirements include, but are not limited to the following specialized security screenings: \nMicrosoft Cloud Background Check: This position will be required to pass the Microsoft Cloud Background Check upon hire/transfer and every two years thereafter.\nPreferred Qualifications:\nMaster's Degree in Computer Science or related technical field with proven experience coding in languages including, but not limited to, Java, C++, C# or object-oriented programming\nOR Bachelor's Degree in Computer Science or related technical field AND 2+ years technical engineering experience with coding in languages including, but not limited to, Java, C++, C# or object-oriented programming\nOR equivalent experience.\n1+ years of experience developing, deploying, monitoring and shipping scalable cloud services. \nCustomer passion, accountability, and drive to take on initiatives and accomplish goals.\nAn entrepreneurial spirit with a can-do attitude: Self-starter, project finisher and adaptable.\nDesign and problem-solving skills, with a bias for designing at scale.\nExperience at shipping a large scale, commercial, online-software solutions.\n \n\n#azurecorejobs #EiP #IC2SWE\n\n\n\nSoftware Engineering IC2 - The typical base pay range for this role across the U.S. is USD $84,200 - $165,200 per year. There is a different range applicable to specific work locations, within the San Francisco Bay area and New York City metropolitan area, and the base pay range for this role in those locations is USD $109,000 - $180,400 per year.\n\nCertain roles may be eligible for benefits and other compensation. Find additional benefits and pay information here:\nhttps://careers.microsoft.com/us/en/us-corporate-pay\n\n\nThis position will be open for a minimum of 5 days, with applications accepted on an ongoing basis until the position is filled.\n\n\n\nMicrosoft is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, ancestry, citizenship, color, family or medical care leave, gender identity or expression, genetic information, immigration status, marital status, medical condition, national origin, physical or mental disability, political affiliation, protected veteran or military status, race, ethnicity, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, or any other characteristic protected by applicable local laws, regulations and ordinances. If you need assistance with religious accommodations and/or a reasonable accommodation due to a disability during the application process, read more about requesting accommodations.\n\n	200023528	Remote	ACTIVE	Software Engineer	7
32	2026-02-17 17:26:00.997028	AAA Life Insurance Company	Sai Teja Mukkera\nWarrensburg, MO\n9139639317\nsaitejamukkera@gmail.com\nhttps://www.linkedin.com/in/saiteja-mukkera\n\nFebruary 17, 2026\nHiring Manager\nAAA Life Insurance Company\n17600 North Laurel Park Drive, Livonia, MI 48152\n\nRe: Application for Software Engineer I (Job ID: ID2026-2076)\n\nDear Hiring Manager,\nI am writing to express my strong interest in the Software Engineer I position at AAA Life Insurance Company. With a Master of Science in Computer Science from the University of Central Missouri (GPA 4.0) and over two years of hands-on experience in full-stack Java development, I have built a career foundation focused on designing scalable, high-performance software solutions. Having followed AAA Life’s legacy of earning policyholder trust since 1969, I am eager to contribute to a team that prioritizes reliability, security, and technical excellence in the life insurance and annuity space.\n\nIn my previous role as a Software Engineer at Cognizant, I specialized in developing and maintaining high-availability microservices using Java and Spring Boot. I successfully led a performance optimization initiative that reduced API payload sizes by 40% using DTO patterns, which significantly improved network throughput for internal stakeholders. I also took ownership of technical aspects of our CI/CD pipeline, utilizing GitHub Actions and SonarQube to automate build and deployment processes. These experiences align directly with AAA Life's focus on maintaining predictable and high-quality software in an Agile environment.\n\nMy background also emphasizes the rigorous quality standards required for financial and insurance systems. I achieved 90% code coverage across enterprise modules by architecting automated unit testing frameworks with JUnit and Mockito. During my Master's program, I studied Software Testing & Quality Assurance and Advanced Application Programming in Java, which allows me to implement robust input validation and remediate security vulnerabilities with a deep understanding of PCI DSS requirements. I am confident in my ability to translate complex business requirements into creative technology solutions while navigating the full system architecture.\n\nI am highly proficient in Java, Spring Boot, React, and SQL, and I am comfortable working with containerization tools like Docker and cloud environments such as AWS. My experience diagnosing production incidents using Splunk and managing tasks via JIRA has prepared me to be a productive member of AAA Life’s hybrid technical team. I am particularly drawn to this role because of AAA Life’s commitment to a diverse and inclusive culture and the opportunity to work under the guidance of senior engineers to further enhance the enterprise systems.\n\nThank you for your time and consideration. I look forward to the possibility of discussing how my technical background and dedication to quality can contribute to the continued success and stability of the software engineering team at AAA Life.\n\nSincerely,\nSai Teja Mukkera\nhttps://www.saitejamukkera.dev\nhttps://www.github.com/saitejamukkera	%-------------------------\n% Resume in Latex (ATS Optimized) - 1 Page Jobright Style (Text Only)\n%------------------------\n\n\\documentclass[letterpaper,10pt]{article}\n\n\\usepackage{latexsym}\n\\usepackage[empty]{fullpage}\n\\usepackage{titlesec}\n\\usepackage[usenames,dvipsnames]{color}\n\\usepackage{enumitem}\n\\usepackage[hidelinks]{hyperref}\n\\usepackage{fancyhdr}\n\\usepackage[english]{babel}\n\\usepackage{tabularx}\n\\input{glyphtounicode}\n\n\\pagestyle{fancy}\n\\fancyhf{}\n\\fancyfoot{}\n\\renewcommand{\\headrulewidth}{0pt}\n\\renewcommand{\\footrulewidth}{0pt}\n\n% MARGINS (ATS-safe, 1-page)\n\\addtolength{\\oddsidemargin}{-0.5in}\n\\addtolength{\\evensidemargin}{-0.5in}\n\\addtolength{\\textwidth}{1in}\n\\addtolength{\\topmargin}{-0.6in}\n\\addtolength{\\textheight}{1.1in}\n\n\\urlstyle{same}\n\\raggedb