JobRadar (Full-Stack Application) $|$ \\href{https://job-radar.vercel.app}{\\underline{Live}} $|$ \\href{https://github.com/saitejamukkera/job-portal-fullstack-mern}{\\underline{GitHub}}}{Oct 2024 -- Jan 2025}\n  {\\small JavaScript, Node.js, React, MongoDB, Express.js, Redux Toolkit}{}\n  \\resumeItemListStart\n    \\resumeItem{Engineered a scalable Job Board platform using the \\textbf{MERN stack}, implementing \\textbf{RBAC} for Recruiters/Applicants.}\n    \\resumeItem{Developed \\textbf{RESTful APIs} with \\textbf{Express.js} and \\textbf{MongoDB}, enabling advanced filtering and reducing latency by 30\\%.}\n    \\resumeItem{Implemented secure authentication using \\textbf{JWT} and \\textbf{Bcrypt}, managing state with \\textbf{Redux Toolkit}.}\n  \\resumeItemListEnd\n\n\\resumeSubHeadingListEnd\n\n%-----------TECHNICAL SKILLS-----------\n\\section{Technical Skills}\n\\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=0.15in, label={}, itemsep=2pt]\n\\small{\\item{\n \\textbf{Programming Languages}{: Java, SQL, JavaScript, TypeScript, Python} \\\\\n \\textbf{Backend Technologies}{: Spring Boot, Microservices (SOA), RESTful APIs, Node.js, Express.js} \\\\\n \\textbf{Frontend Technologies}{: React, Redux Toolkit, TailwindCSS, HTML5, CSS3, Bootstrap} \\\\\n \\textbf{Databases \\& Cloud}{: PostgreSQL, MongoDB, MySQL, AWS (EC2, S3, RDS), Vercel} \\\\\n \\textbf{DevOps \\& Automation}{: Docker, GitHub Actions, Jenkins, TDD (JUnit, Mockito), Splunk, Agile (Scrum)} \\\\\n \\textbf{IDEs}{: IntelliJ IDEA, VS Code, Eclipse, Cursor, Claude Code}\n}}\n\\end{itemize}\n\n\\end{document}	Software Engineer, Global Banking & Markets, Investment Banking\nDallas, Texas, United States\nJob Description\nWhat We Do\n\nAt Goldman Sachs, our Engineers don't just make things - we make things possible.  Change the world by connecting people and capital with ideas.  Solve the most challenging and pressing engineering problems for our clients.  Join our engineering teams that build massively scalable software and systems, architect low latency infrastructure solutions, proactively guard against cyber threats, and leverage machine learning alongside financial engineering to continuously turn data into action.  Create new businesses, transform finance, and explore a world of opportunity at the speed of markets.\n\nGoldman Sachs Engineers are innovators and problem-solvers, building solutions in risk management, big data, mobile and more. We look for creative collaborators who evolve, adapt to change and thrive in a fast-paced global environment. Want to push the limit of digital possibilities?  Start here.\n\nWithin our Global Banking & Markets business, Investment Banking (IB) works on some of the most complex financial challenges and transactions in the market today. Whether advising on a merger, providing financial solutions for an acquisition, or structuring an initial public offering, we handle projects that help clients at major milestones. We work with corporations, pension funds, financial sponsors, and governments and are a team of strong analytical thinkers with a passion for producing out-of-the-box ideas.\n\nWithin IB, our engineers are responsible for building next generation digital solutions and automation for banking that consists of a set of well-integrated platforms and allows us to serve our bankers and clients better.\n\n \n\nWho We Look For\n\nAs part of our global team, you will work on various technologies and components as an application developer. Your role includes specification, development, as well as the testing and roll-out of new features focusing on code quality, automation, testability and security. You will be able to contribute to our vision, roadmap, and world-class engineering culture, while integrating business value and client experience within the team.\n\nWe expect a successful candidate to have excellent communication skills, deliver high quality software, and to be passionate about cutting edge engineering. \n\n \n\nHow You Will Fulfill Your Potential\n\nManage multiple tasks and use sound judgment when prioritizing.\nCollaborate with global cross functional teams in building customer-centric products.\nUtilize exceptional analytical skills and ability to apply knowledge and experience in decision-making to arrive at creative and commercial solutions.\nAnalyze existing software implementations to identify areas of improvement and provide deadline estimates for implementing new features.\nEstablish trusted partnerships with peers, product heads, and executive-level stakeholders.\nLeverage technology to deliver business value.\n \n\nBasic Qualifications\n\nAdvanced degree in Computer Science (or equivalent work experience).\nComfort with Agile operating models (practical experience of Scrum/Kanban).\nExperience leveraging test-driven development methodologies.\nTeam oriented; strong interpersonal and communication skills.\nEnergetic, self-directed, and self-motivated.\nMust be passionate about technology and engineering.\nMust be independent and comfortable in a fast paced, ambiguous, and often multi-directional work environment.\n \n\nPreferred Qualifications\n\n1-4 years of relevant professional experience using a modern programming language (preferably Java).\nExperience in Financial Services or Fintech.\nExperience with microservice architectures (SOA).\nExperience with Kafka, MongoDB, Hadoop, Cassandra.\nExperience with SQL databases (PostgreSQL/Oracle/Sybase).\nExperience with AWS/Azure.\n \n\nABOUT GOLDMAN SACHS\n\nAt Goldman Sachs, we commit our people, capital and ideas to help our clients, shareholders and the communities we serve to grow. Founded in 1869, we are a leading global investment banking, securities and investment management firm. Headquartered in New York, we maintain offices around the world. \n\nWe believe who you are makes you better at what you do. We're committed to fostering and advancing diversity and inclusion in our own workplace and beyond by ensuring every individual within our firm has a number of opportunities to grow professionally and personally, from our training and development opportunities and firmwide networks to benefits, wellness and personal finance offerings and mindfulness programs. Learn more about our culture, benefits, and people at GS.com/careers. \n\nWe're committed to finding reasonable accommodations for candidates with special needs or disabilities during our recruiting process. Learn more: https://www.goldmansachs.com/careers/footer/disability-statement.html\n\n© The Goldman Sachs Group, Inc., 2026. All rights reserved.\n\nJob Info\nJob Identification\n161630\nJob Category\nAssociate\nPosting Date\n02/17/2026, 07:59 PM\nLocations\n Dallas, Texas, United States\nApply Now\n	161630	Dallas, TX	ACTIVE	Software Engineer, Global Banking & Markets, Investment Banking	7
67	2026-02-21 00:15:45.570117	PayPal	Sai Teja Mukkera\nWarrensburg, MO\n9139639317\nsaitejamukkera@gmail.com\nhttps://www.linkedin.com/in/saiteja-mukkera\n\nFebruary 21, 2026\nHiring Manager\nPayPal\nSan Jose, CA\n\nRe: Application for Software Engineer - Java (Job ID: R0133240)\n\nDear Hiring Manager,\nI am writing to express my strong interest in the Software Engineer (Java) position at PayPal. Having recently completed my Master of Science in Computer Science with a 4.0 GPA and possessing over two years of professional experience in enterprise Java development, I am eager to contribute to a company that has spent 25 years revolutionizing global commerce. My background in building high-availability microservices using Spring Boot, coupled with my commitment to writing clean, maintainable code, aligns perfectly with PayPal’s mission of providing secure and seamless digital payment solutions for hundreds of millions of users worldwide.\n\nDuring my tenure at Cognizant, I focused on developing and optimizing backend components within a Service-Oriented Architecture. I successfully refactored API structures using DTO patterns to reduce JSON payload sizes by 40%, significantly improving network throughput for end-users. I also played a key role in ensuring application stability by resolving over 40 production incidents using Splunk for log analysis and maintaining a 90% code coverage standard through JUnit and Mockito. These experiences taught me the importance of reliability and performance in large-scale systems, values that I know are central to PayPal’s engineering culture.\n\nIn addition to my professional experience, my academic journey provided me with deep theoretical and practical insights into building complex software. During my Master's program, I studied Advanced Application Programming in Java, which allows me to implement sophisticated design patterns and concurrency models effectively. Furthermore, my coursework in Advanced Computer Networking & Security has equipped me with a robust understanding of how to secure distributed systems—a critical competency when managing the sensitive transactional data that moves through PayPal’s global network every day.\n\nMy technical toolkit includes extensive experience with Java, Spring Boot, and RESTful web services, as well as hands-on exposure to both relational databases like PostgreSQL and NoSQL solutions like MongoDB. I am well-versed in Agile methodologies and CI/CD workflows using Git and GitHub Actions, ensuring that I can integrate quickly into your development team. I am particularly drawn to PayPal because of your commitment to innovation and inclusion, and I am excited by the prospect of solving the unique technical challenges associated with processing millions of secure transactions in a high-performance environment.\n\nThank you for your time and consideration. I look forward to the possibility of discussing how my technical background and passion for fintech can contribute to the continued success of the PayPal engineering team.\n\nSincerely,\nSai Teja Mukkera\nhttps://www.saitejamukkera.dev\nhttps://www.github.com/saitejamukkera	%-------------------------\n% Resume in Latex (ATS Optimized) - 1 Page Jobright Style + Icons\n%------------------------\n\n\\documentclass[letterpaper,10pt]{article}\n\n\\usepackage{latexsym}\n\\usepackage[empty]{fullpage}\n\\usepackage{titlesec}\n\\usepackage{marvosym}\n\\usepackage[usenames,dvipsnames]{color}\n\\usepackage{enumitem}\n\\usepackage[hidelinks]{hyperref}\n\\usepackage{fancyhdr}\n\\usepackage{fontawesome5}\n\\usepackage[english]{babel}\n\\usepackage{tabularx}\n\\input{glyphtounicode}\n\n\\pagestyle{fancy}\n\\fancyhf{}\n\\fancyfoot{}\n\\renewcommand{\\headrulewidth}{0pt}\n\\renewcommand{\\footrulewidth}{0pt}\n\n% MARGINS (slightly tighter but ATS-safe)\n\\addtolength{\\oddsidemargin}{-0.5in}\n\\addtolength{\\evensidemargin}{-0.5in}\n\\addtolength{\\textwidth}{1in}\n\\addtolength{\\topmargin}{-0.6in}\n\\addtolength{\\tex