ured public endpoints with a \\textbf{Caddy} reverse proxy, automating HTTPS and service orchestration.}\n    \\resumeItem{Enabled AI-powered features by integrating a \\textbf{Large Language Model (LLM)} via the Gemini API, supporting intelligent resume analysis and job matching.}\n  \\resumeItemListEnd\n\n\\resumeSubheading\n  {JobRadar (Full-Stack Application) $|$ \\hspace{1pt} \\href{https://job-radar.vercel.app}{\\faLink} \\hspace{2pt} \\href{https://github.com/saitejamukkera/job-portal-fullstack-mern}{\\faGithub}}{Oct 2024 -- Jan 2025}\n  {JavaScript, Node.js, React, MongoDB, Express.js, Redux Toolkit}{}\n  \\resumeItemListStart\n    \\resumeItem{Engineered a scalable Job Board platform using the \\textbf{MERN stack}, implementing \\textbf{RBAC} for Recruiters/Applicants.}\n    \\resumeItem{Developed \\textbf{RESTful APIs} with \\textbf{Express.js} and \\textbf{MongoDB}, enabling advanced filtering and reducing latency by 30\\%.}\n    \\resumeItem{Implemented secure authentication using \\textbf{JWT} and \\textbf{Bcrypt}, managing state with \\textbf{Redux Toolkit}.}\n  \\resumeItemListEnd\n\n\\resumeSubHeadingListEnd\n\n%-----------TECHNICAL SKILLS-----------\n\\section{Technical Skills}\n\\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=0.15in, label={}, itemsep=2pt]\n\\small{\\item{\n \\textbf{Programming Languages}{: Java, JavaScript, TypeScript, SQL, Python} \\\\\n \\textbf{Backend Technologies}{: Spring Boot, RESTful APIs, Node.js, Express.js, Microservices, SOA} \\\\\n \\textbf{Frontend Technologies}{: React, Redux, HTML5, CSS3, Bootstrap, TailwindCSS} \\\\\n \\textbf{Databases \\& Cloud}{: PostgreSQL, MongoDB, MySQL, Cassandra, AWS (EC2, S3, RDS), Vercel} \\\\\n \\textbf{DevOps, AI \\& Tools}{: Docker, Git, GitHub Actions, Jenkins, Splunk, SonarQube, Agile, Scrum} \\\\\n \\textbf{IDEs}{: IntelliJ IDEA, Eclipse, Cursor, VS Code, Claude Code}\n}}\n\\end{itemize}\n\n\\end{document}	Software Engineer - Java\nApply\nlocations\nSan Jose, California, United States of America\ntime type\nFull time\nposted on\nPosted Today\njob requisition id\nR0133240\nThe Company\n\nPayPal has been revolutionizing commerce globally for more than 25 years. Creating innovative experiences that make moving money, selling, and shopping simple, personalized, and secure, PayPal empowers consumers and businesses in approximately 200 markets to join and thrive in the global economy. \n\nWe operate a global, two-sided network at scale that connects hundreds of millions of merchants and consumers. We help merchants and consumers connect, transact, and complete payments, whether they are online or in person. PayPal is more than a connection to third-party payment networks. We provide proprietary payment solutions accepted by merchants that enable the completion of payments on our platform on behalf of our customers.\n\nWe offer our customers the flexibility to use their accounts to purchase and receive payments for goods and services, as well as the ability to transfer and withdraw funds. We enable consumers to exchange funds more safely with merchants using a variety of funding sources, which may include a bank account, a PayPal or Venmo account balance, PayPal and Venmo branded credit products, a credit card, a debit card, certain cryptocurrencies, or other stored value products such as gift cards, and eligible credit card rewards.  Our PayPal, Venmo, and Xoom products also make it safer and simpler for friends and family to transfer funds to each other. We offer merchants an end-to-end payments solution that provides authorization and settlement capabilities, as well as instant access to funds and payouts. We also help merchants connect with their customers, process exchanges and returns, and manage risk. We enable consumers to engage in cross-border shopping and merchants to extend their global reach while reducing the complexity and friction involved in enabling cross-border trade. \n\nOur beliefs are the foundation for how we conduct business every day.  We live each day guided by our core values of Inclusion, Innovation, Collaboration, and Wellness. Together, our values ensure that we work together as one global team with our customers at the center of everything we do – and they push us to ensure we take care of ourselves, each other, and our communities.\n\nJob Summary:\n\nAt PayPal, Backend Software Engineers help build and maintain the systems that power millions of secure transactions every day. As a Backend Software Engineer (Java), you’ll collaborate with experienced engineers to design, develop, and optimize backend components that ensure performance, reliability, and scalability across our global payment platform. You’ll write clean, efficient Java code, follow established development practices, and participate in code reviews to continuously learn and improve. This role offers the opportunity to grow your technical expertise while contributing to PayPal’s mission of enabling secure, seamless digital payments worldwide.\nJob Description:\n\nEssential Responsibilities: \n\nImplements tasks within the Software Development Lifecycle (SDLC), receiving structure and oversight from more experienced staff\nFollows well-established internal conventions and standard procedures\nUnderstands internal standards & processes an applies them to make technical decisions\nCollaborates with peers, manager, and project lead to gain understanding of tasks and review solutions\nMay contribute to code & design reviews\nExpected Qualifications:\n\n1+ years relevant experience and a Bachelor’s degree OR Any equivalent combination of education and experience.\nAdditional Responsibilities & Preferred Qualifications:\n\nAdditional Qualifications: \n\nStrong foundation in programming concepts, algorithms, and data structures. \n\nExperience with backend development using Java and frameworks such as Spring Boot or Micronaut. \n\nUnderstanding of RESTful web services and Service-Oriented Architecture (SOA) principles. \n\nFamiliarity with relational and NoSQL databases (e.g., MySQL, PostgreSQL, MongoDB, Cassandra). \n\nExposure to version control systems (e.g., Git) and collaborative development workflows (e.g., Agile, CI/CD). \n\nPreferred Qualifications: \n\nInterest in large-scale, high-performance distributed systems. \n\nAwareness of the payment processing industry and related compliance or regulatory standards. \n\nExposure to cloud platforms such as AWS, GCP, or Azure. \n\nContributions to open-source projects or participation in developer communities. \n\nSubsidiary:\n\nPayPal\nTravel Percent:\n\n0\n-\n\nThe base pay for this role will depend on where you work and the relevant experience and expertise you bring. The expected range of pay for this role by location is:\nPrimary Location | Pay Range:\n\nSan Jose, California | ($116,500.00 - $173,250.00 Annually)\nAdditional Location(s) | Pay Range:\n\nNo other locations are assigned to this requisition currently.\nAdditional compensation for this role may include an annual performance bonus, equity, or other incentive compensation, as applicable.\nPayPal does not charge candidates any fees for courses, applications, resume reviews, interviews, background checks, or onboarding. Any such request is a red flag and likely part of a scam. To learn more about how to identify and avoid recruitment fraud please visit https://careers.pypl.com/contact-us.\n\nFor the majority of employees, PayPal's balanced hybrid work model offers 3 days in the office for effective in-person collaboration and 2 days at your choice of either the PayPal office or your home workspace, ensuring that you equally have the benefits and conveniences of both locations.\n\nOur Benefits:\n\nAt PayPal, we’re committed to building an equitable and inclusive global economy. And we can’t do this without our most important asset-you. That’s why we offer comprehensive, choice-based programs, to support all aspects of personal wellbeing—physical, emotional, and financial—delivering meaningful value where it matters most. We strive to create a flexible, balanced work culture with a holistic approach to benefits, including generous paid time off, healthcare coverage for you and your family, and resources to create financial security and support your mental health.\n\nWho We Are:\n\nClick Here to learn more about our culture and community.\n\nCommitment to Diversity and Inclusion  \n\nPayPal provides equal employment opportunity (EEO) to all persons regardless of age, color, national origin, citizenship status, physical or mental disability, race, religion, creed, gender, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity and/or expression, genetic information, marital status, status with regard to public assistance, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state, or local law.  In addition, PayPal will provide reasonable accommodations for qualified individuals with disabilities.  If you are unable to submit an application because of incompatible assistive technology or a disability, please contact us at paypalglobaltalentacquisition@paypal.com. \n\nBelonging at PayPal: \n\nOur employees are central to advancing our mission, and we strive to create an environment where everyone can do their best work with a sense of purpose and belonging. Belonging at PayPal means creating a workplace with a sense of acceptance and security where all employees feel included and valued. We are proud to have a diverse workforce reflective of the merchants, consumers, and communities that we serve, and we continue to take tangible actions to cultivate inclusivity and belonging at PayPal.\n\nAny general requests for consideration of your skills, please Join our Talent Community. \n\nWe know the confidence gap and imposter syndrome can get in the way of meeting spectacular candidates. Please don’t hesitate to apply.\n\n	R0133240	San Jose, CA	ACTIVE	Software Engineer - Java	7
59	2026-02-19 12:16:39.464759	CVS Health	Sai Teja Mukkera\nWarrensburg, MO\n9139639317\nsaitejamukkera@gmail.com\nhttps://www.linkedin.com/in/saiteja-mukkera\n\nFebruary 19, 2026\nHiring Manager\nCVS Health\nRichardson, TX\n\nRe: Application for Full Stack Software Development Engineer (Java) (Job ID: R0826568)\n\nDear Hiring Manager,\nI am writing to express my strong interest in the Full Stack Software Development Engineer position within the Digital Enterprise team at CVS Health. With a Master of Science in Computer Science and a perfect 4.0 GPA, combined with over three years of professional experience at Cognizant, I have developed a deep expertise in building resilient enterprise-scale applications. My background is rooted in Java, Spring Boot, and React, and I am eager to apply my technical skills to help CVS Health shape a more connected and compassionate health experience through innovative digital identity solutions.\n\nThroughout my tenure as a Software Engineer, I have consistently delivered efficient, high-quality solutions across the full software development life cycle. At Cognizant, I designed and maintained microservices using Spring Boot and AWS that supported over 10,000 users with exceptional uptime. I have a proven track record of optimizing performance, such as reducing API response times by 25% through efficient DTO patterns and query optimization. Furthermore, my experience blending backend robustness with interactive React frontends has allowed me to build seamless, user-centric interfaces that align perfectly with the "Full Stack" requirements of your healthcare identity domain.\n\nI am particularly adept at operating within SAFe Agile environments and leveraging DevOps tools like Jenkins and GitHub Actions to automate CI/CD pipelines. My focus on reliability is demonstrated by my commitment to unit testing and code quality, where I increased test coverage to 90% using JUnit 5. I am also experienced in monitoring and troubleshooting complex systems using Splunk, ensuring that digital products remain stable and secure after deployment. These experiences have prepared me to mitigate risks and contribute to the high standards of safety and quality that CVS Health prioritizes.\n\nMy technical foundation is further strengthened by my graduate studies at the University of Central Missouri. During my Master's program, I studied Advanced Applications Programming in Java, which allows me to architect complex, multi-tiered enterprise systems that are both scalable and maintainable. Additionally, my coursework in Software Testing and Quality Assurance has provided me with a rigorous framework for conducting system testing and debugging, ensuring that the digital solutions I build are reliable and meet the highest industry standards for healthcare technology. My proficiency in Java/J2EE, React, RESTful services, and AWS, combined with my knowledge of OAuth2 and PostgreSQL, makes me a strong fit for your team’s current technical needs.\n\nI am enthusiastic about the opportunity to join CVS Health, a company that leads the industry in simplifying healthcare for individuals and communities. I am confident that my blend of full-stack technical proficiency, problem-solving mindset, and academic excellence will allow me to make immediate and meaningful contributions to your Digital Enterprise projects.\n\nThank you for your time and consideration. I look forward to the possibility of discussing how I can contribute to the continued innovation and stability of CVS Health’s digital solutions.\n\nSincerely,\nSai Teja Mukkera\nhttps://www.saitejamukkera.dev\nhttps://www.github.com/saitejamukkera	%-------------------------\n% Resume in Latex (ATS Optimized) - 1 Page Jobright Style (Text Only)\n%------------------------\n\n\\documentclass[a4paper,10pt]{article}\n\n\\usepackage{latexsym}\n\\usepackage[empty]{fullpage}\n\\usepackage{titlesec}\n\\usepackage[usenames,dvipsnames]{color}\n\\usepackage{enumitem}\n\\usepackage[hidel