ution, as well as identify and properly mitigate any risks to the product before deployment to production.\nUnderstand business requirements and translate them into engineering solutions\nWrite and execute unit tests, conduct code reviews, debug, and troubleshoot issues to ensure the reliability and stability of digital solutions\nLeverage advanced programming skills to design and implement complex features, optimize performance, and ensure code efficiency\nIntegrate various software components or systems, ensuring seamless communication and interoperability between different parts of the digital solutions\nParticipate in SAFe agile methodologies, attends meetings, and contributes to project planning and progress tracking\nExplore new tools, frameworks, and techniques to improve digital solutions and drive innovation within the development team\nCreate and maintain technical documentation, including system designs, architecture diagrams, code documentation, and other relevant documentation while sharing their knowledge and expertise with team members, ensuring effective knowledge transfer and collaboration\n\nRequired Qualifications\n\nThis is a hybrid position that requires 2-3 days per week in the office. Office locations are Scottsdale, AZ and Richardson, TX. Candidates must live a commutable distance to either of these locations.\n2+ years of software development experience in building enterprise/web/cloud applications\n2+ years of experience in programming languages using Java/J2EE, Spring Boot and Spring MVC\n2+ years of experience working in React JS OR Angular UI applications\n2+ years of experience with building APIs and services using REST\n2+ years of experience working with DevOps tools/processes for CICD (i.e. Jenkins, Octopus)\n2+ years of experience in build, testing, and deploying code to run on cloud infrastructure (AWS/GCP/Azure)\n2+ years of experience with Scrum/Agile development methodologies\n1+ years of experience working with RDBMS databases 