41	2026-02-17 23:47:27.634668	Cisco	Sai Teja Mukkera\nWarrensburg, MO\n9139639317\nsaitejamukkera@gmail.com\nhttps://www.linkedin.com/in/saiteja-mukkera\n\nFebruary 17, 2026\nHiring Manager\nCisco\n170 West Tasman Dr.\nSan Jose, CA 95134\n\nRe: Application for Software Engineer Backend/Platform Systems I (Job ID: 2000046)\n\nDear Hiring Manager,\nI am writing to express my strong interest in the Software Engineer Backend/Platform Systems I position at Cisco. Having recently completed my Master of Science in Computer Science with a 4.0 GPA and possessing over two years of professional experience as a Software Engineer at Cognizant, I am eager to contribute to Cisco’s mission of building AI-driven data infrastructure. My background is rooted in developing scalable Java-based microservices and robust backend platforms that power business-critical initiatives. I have long admired Cisco’s 40-year legacy of fearless innovation, and I am excited by the opportunity to apply my technical curiosity to your evolving intelligent automation platforms.\n\nDuring my tenure at Cognizant, I focused on enhancing platform stability and backend efficiency. I successfully refactored API structures for high-concurrency microservices using Spring Boot, which resulted in a 40% reduction in JSON payload sizes and significantly improved network throughput. My experience extends to diagnosing complex production incidents in Linux environments using tools like Splunk, where I resolved over 40 critical defects to maintain 99.9% system uptime. I also spearheaded the expansion of automated testing suites to 90% code coverage, ensuring that every deployment through our CI/CD pipelines was reliable and met strict quality gates.\n\nFurthermore, my technical projects, such as TrackHire AI, demonstrate my ability to architect full-stack solutions and integrate emerging technologies. I built a containerized backend using Docker and PostgreSQL, while integrating Large Language Models (LLMs) to provide i