t clients such as Stash, Betterment, SoFi, and Webull, and more than 20 million of our clients' customers. \n\nCollectively, AFS creates an environment in which companies with the biggest ideas in fintech are empowered to change the world. As a global organization, we have offices in Austin, Dallas, Chicago, New York, Portland, Belfast, and Manila.\n\nIf you are seeking a fast-paced and entrepreneurial environment where you'll have the opportunity to make an immediate impact, and you have the guts to change everything, this is the place for you. \n\nAFS has received a number of prestigious industry awards, including:\n\n2021, 2020, 2019, and 2018 Best Wealth Management Company - presented by Fintech Breakthrough Awards\n\n2021 Most Innovative Companies - presented by Fast Company\n\n2021 Best API & Best Trading Technology - presented by Global Fintech Awards\n\nABOUT THIS ROLE\n\nThis is an incredible opportunity for Software Engineer I who will work closely with software development and business teams building products and services for customers of Apex Fintech Solutions' suite of financial back office solutions.  \n\n\nDuties/Responsibilities\n\nWorking with a variety of languages/frameworks, such as Java, Go, Python and technologies such as RDBMS, Kubernetes, and Docker, Google Cloud Platform \n\nDesigning, developing, testing, deploying, maintaining and improving software \n\nBuilding resilient, self-scaling, self-healing services that allow you to sleep through the night \n\nWriting high-quality, well-tested code. Maintaining high code-quality standards across your team via code reviews \n\nAttending training and expand domain knowledge on Accounts creation and Maintenance \n\nEncouraging innovation by questioning business processes throughout the company \n\nEducation and/or Experience\n\nBachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering, Electrical or Computer Engineering, or a related field. \n\n2+ years of prior work experience preferred\n\nRequired Skills/Abilities\n\nExperience of software development skills in a modern object-oriented programming language ideally Java / Go, Python considered a plus, an RDBMS or SQL, and the ability to learn new languages and technologies quickly \n\nExcellent problem-solving skills with high attention to detail \n\nEffective communication skills \n\nPrevious knowledge in financial markets isn’t required, but interest is a plus \n\nAdaptability: while you enjoy establishing process and standards, you understand the need to be flexible and enjoy trying new things \n\nWork Environment\n\nThis job operates operates in hybrid, office environment 3 days per week.\n\n#engineering #entry-level #full-time #LI-SD1 #APEX\n\n​Please note this job description is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties, or responsibilities required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities, and activities may change at any time with or without notice.\n\nOur Rewards\n\nWe offer a robust package of employee perks and benefits, including healthcare benefits (medical, dental and vision, EAP), competitive PTO, 401k match, parental leave, and HSA contribution match. We also provide our employees with a paid subscription to the Calm app and offer generous external learning and tuition reimbursement benefits. At AFS, we offer a hybrid work schedule for most roles that allows employees to have the flexibility of working from home and one of our primary offices.\n\nEEO Statement\n\nApex Fintech Solutions is an equal opportunity employer that does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy, sexual orientation, and gender identity), national origin, age, disability, veteran status, marital status, or any other protected characteristic. Our hiring practices ensure that all qualified applicants receive fair consideration without regard to these characteristics.\n\nDisability Statement\n\nApex Fintech Solutions is committed to creating an inclusive and accessible workplace for all candidates, including those with disabilities. We are dedicated to ensuring equal employment opportunities and providing reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities. If you require reasonable accommodations to participate in the application or interview process, please submit your request via the Candidate Accommodation Requests Form. We will work with you to provide the necessary accommodations to ensure your full participation in our hiring process.\n\nRecommended Jobs\nSecurity Engineering Manager\nClient Services Analyst\nStaff Enterprise Architect, Solutions Architecture\nSenior Kubernetes Platform Engineer\nSenior Manager, Software Engineering\nGet Notified of Open Positions!\nSign up to receive emails when Apex Fintech Solutions posts open positions you might be interested in:\nFirst Name *\n\nLast Name *\n\nEmail *\n\nIf you click to sign-up above; you will be added to the Apex Fintech Solutions talent network. Your information will not be shared or sold. *\n\nApex Fintech Solutions search bar\nSearch for items\n\nWho We Serve\nEstablished Wealth Management Firms\nEstablished full service broker dealers\nInternational wealth and brokerage firms\nBanks and Credit Unions\nStartups\nConsumer Brands\n401(k) Third-Party Administrators\nCryptocurrency trading platforms\nSelf-clearing firms\nCorporate treasury management\n\nProducts\nAscendOS™ Platform\nAccount Opening and Funding\nClearing and Custody\nWealth Tech\nTrading\n\nDevelopers\nDeveloper Portal\nSandbox\nAscendOS™ Platform\nGoogle Cloud\n\n		Austin, TX	ACTIVE	Software Engineer I	7
68	2026-02-21 01:09:11.990592	PayPal	Sai Teja Mukkera\nWarrensburg, MO\n9139639317\nsaitejamukkera@gmail.com\nhttps://www.linkedin.com/in/saiteja-mukkera\n\nFebruary 21, 2026\nHiring Manager\nPayPal\nSan Jose, CA\n\nRe: Application for Software Engineer (Job ID: R0134877)\n\nDear Hiring Manager,\nI am writing to express my enthusiastic interest in the Software Engineer position within the Customer Success Self-Service team at PayPal. Having recently completed my Master of Science in Computer Science with a 4.0 GPA and possessing over 3.5 years of professional experience in full-stack development, I am eager to contribute to PayPal's mission of revolutionizing commerce. My background in building high-throughput Java microservices and intuitive React-based user interfaces aligns perfectly with your goal of creating seamless messaging experiences for Chat, Inbox, and Email SDKs.\n\nIn my most recent role at Saayam Org, I have been architecting event-driven microservices using Spring Boot and Apache Kafka, focusing on real-time state synchronization which is critical for messaging platforms. I have also engineered responsive frontends using Next.js and TypeScript, prioritizing user-centric design to reduce time-to-interactive metrics. During my tenure at Cognizant, I maintained 6+ Spring Boot microservices and integrated Redis caching to ensure 99.8% availability for over 10,000 users. My experience implementing Spring Security and OAuth2 for distributed services directly supports PayPal’s commitment to secure, high-scale financial transactions.\n\nI am particularly drawn to this role because of the opportunity to blend traditional full-stack engineering with emerging AI and Machine Learning concepts. During my Master's program, I studied Machine Learning and Advanced Application Programming in Java, which allows me to effectively bridge the gap between complex backend logic and intelligent, automated user interactions. I have practical experience integrating LLM APIs for intelligent data analysis in my personal projects, and I am excited to apply these skills to enhance PayPal's self-service capabilities and help users resolve issues independently through innovative AI-driven features.\n\nMy technical foundation is built on Java, Spring WebFlux, React, and TypeScript, complemented by a deep understanding of CI/CD pipelines via GitHub Actions and observability through Splunk and CloudWatch. I am a firm believer in the power of collaboration within Agile environments and am passionate about delivering clean, reliable code that improves the lives of millions. My academic focus on Advanced Comp Networking and Security further ensures that I approach every development task with a security-first mindset, essential for the payments industry.\n\nThank you for your time and consideration. I look forward to the possibility of discussing how I can contribute to the Messaging development team and help shape the next generation of PayPal’s digital experiences.\n\nSincerely,\nSai Teja Mukkera\nhttps://www.saitejamukkera.dev\nhttps://www.github.com/saitejamukkera	\\documentclass[a4paper,10pt]{article}\n\n\\usepackage{latexsym}\n\\usepackage[empty]{fullpage}\n\\usepackage{titlesec}\n\\usepackage[usenames,dvipsnames]{color}\n\\usepackage{enumitem}\n\\usepackage[hidelinks]{hyperref}\n\\usepackage{fancyhdr}\n\\usepackage[english]{babel}\n\\usepackage{tabularx}\n\\input{glyphtounicode}\n\n\\pagestyle{fancy}\n\\fancyhf{}\n\\fancyfoot{}\n\\renewcommand{\\headrulewidth}{0pt}\n\\renewcommand{\\footrulewidth}{0pt}\n\n% MARGINS (ATS-safe, 1-page)\n\\addtolength{\\oddsidemargin}{-0.5in}\n\\addtolength{\\evensidemargin}{-0.5in}\n\\addtolength{\\textwidth}{1in}\n\\addtolength{\\topmargin}{-0.6in}\n\\addtolength{\\textheight}{1.1in}\n\n\\urlstyle{same}\n\\raggedbottom\n\\raggedright\n\\setlength{\\tabcolsep}{0in}\n\n% SECTION FORMATTING\n\\titleformat{\\section}{\n  \\vspace{-10pt}\\scshape\\raggedright\\large\n}{}{0em}{}[\\color{black}\\titlerule \\vspace{-7