educing latency by 30\\%.}\n    \\resumeItem{Implemented secure authentication using \\textbf{JWT} and \\textbf{Bcrypt}, managing state with \\textbf{Redux Toolkit}.}\n  \\resumeItemListEnd\n\n\\resumeSubHeadingListEnd\n\n%-----------TECHNICAL SKILLS-----------\n\\section{Technical Skills}\n\\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=0.15in, label={}, itemsep=2pt]\n\\small{\\item{\n \\textbf{Programming Languages:} Java (Expert), Python, JavaScript, TypeScript, SQL (PostgreSQL, MySQL, NoSQL) \\\\\n \\textbf{Backend Technologies:} Spring Boot, Spring MVC, REST APIs, Apache Kafka, Node.js, Express.js \\\\\n \\textbf{Frontend Technologies:} React, Next.js, Redux, TailwindCSS, HTML5, CSS3, Responsive Design \\\\\n \\textbf{Databases \\& Cloud:} AWS (EC2, S3, RDS, ECS), Vercel, MongoDB, Redis Caching \\\\\n \\textbf{DevOps \\& Monitoring:} Docker, Testcontainers, GitHub Actions, Jenkins, Splunk, CloudWatch, SonarQube \\\\\n \\textbf{IDEs \\& AI:} IntelliJ IDEA, VS Code, Cursor, AI/ML Concepts, Agile Methodologies, Code Review\n}}\n\\end{itemize}\n\n\\end{document}	Associate Software Development Engineer (Conversion)\nApply\nremote type\nRemote/Hybrid\nlocations\nCT - Hartford\ntime type\nFull time\nposted on\nPosted Today\ntime left to apply\nEnd Date: February 20, 2026 (6 hours left to apply)\njob requisition id\nR0835835\nWe’re building a world of health around every individual — shaping a more connected, convenient and compassionate health experience. At CVS Health®, you’ll be surrounded by passionate colleagues who care deeply, innovate with purpose, hold ourselves accountable and prioritize safety and quality in everything we do. Join us and be part of something bigger – helping to simplify health care one person, one family and one community at a time.\n\nPosition Summary\n\nWe are looking for an Associate Microservices Engineer to build efficient and scalable distributed systems. The ideal candidate should have strong knowledge in Java/Python frameworks, SQL/NoSQL Databases, Cloud architectures. You will be responsible for developing and maintaining high-performance solutions that enable real-time and batch processing.\n\nIf you are passionate about building high-performance data solutions and want to work on cutting-edge technologies using AI, we’d love to hear from you!\n\nKey Responsibilities:\n\nDevelop and maintain high-performance microservices using Java or Python.\nDevelop REST APIs using Spring MVC Framework, Spring Boot Framework, Apache Camel, other tech stacks (Open source and proprietary)\nCollaborate with Offshore teams to manage deliverables, conduct code reviews, and maintain best practices\nEnsure code quality through automated testing (unit, integration), logging, monitoring and alerting\nTroubleshoot performance issues and optimize microservices interactions and database access\nParticipate in architecture discussions and technical design sessions\nRequired Qualifications\n\n4 years of relevant background/course work in Computer Science/Engineering\nPreferred Qualifications\n\nStrong understanding of Software Engineering standards and concepts especially with Object-Oriented languages like Java\nUnderstanding of database technologies and languages SQL/NoSQL\nBachelor’s degree in computer science/engineering\nExcellent communication and Stakeholder management skills\nEducation\n\nBachelor’s degree in relevant engineering field (Computer Science)\n\nAnticipated Weekly Hours\n\n40\nTime Type\n\nFull time\nPay Range\n\nThe typical pay range for this role is:\n\n$32.69 - $65.36\nThis pay range represents the base hourly rate or base annual full-time salary for all positions in the job grade within which this position falls.  The actual base salary offer will depend on a variety of factors including experience, education, geography and other relevant factors.  This position is eligible for a CVS Health bonus, commission or short-term incentive program in addition to the base pay range listed above. \n \n\nOur people fuel our future. Our teams reflect the customers, patients, members and communities we serve and we are committed to fostering a workplace where every colleague feels valued and that they belong.\n\nGreat benefits for great people\n\nWe take pride in our comprehensive and competitive mix of pay and benefits – investing in the physical, emotional and financial wellness of our colleagues and their families to help them be the healthiest they can be. In addition to our competitive wages, our great benefits include:\n\nAffordable medical plan options, a 401(k) plan (including matching company contributions), and an employee stock purchase plan.\n\nNo-cost programs for all colleagues including wellness screenings, tobacco cessation and weight management programs, confidential counseling and financial coaching.\n\nBenefit solutions that address the different needs and preferences of our colleagues including paid time off, flexible work schedules, family leave, dependent care resources, colleague assistance programs, tuition assistance, retiree medical access and many other benefits depending on eligibility.\n\nFor more information, visit https://jobs.cvshealth.com/us/en/benefits\n\nWe anticipate the application window for this opening will close on\nQualified applicants with arrest or conviction records will be considered for employment in accordance with all federal, state and local laws.\n\n	R0835835	Hartford, CT	REJECTED	Associate Software Development Engineer (Conversion)	7
51	2026-02-18 12:45:54.483782	Crate & Barrel	Sai Teja Mukkera\nWarrensburg, MO\n9139639317\nsaitejamukkera@gmail.com\nhttps://www.linkedin.com/in/saiteja-mukkera\n\nFebruary 18, 2026\nHiring Manager\nCrate & Barrel\n\nRe: Application for Software Engineer, Payments (Job ID: R22363)\n\nDear Hiring Manager,\nI am writing to express my strong interest in the Software Engineer position on the Payments team at Crate & Barrel. With a Master of Science in Computer Science from the University of Central Missouri, where I maintained a 4.0 GPA, and over three years of professional experience as a Software Engineer at Cognizant, I have developed a deep proficiency in building secure, scalable backend systems using Java and Spring Boot. I have long admired Crate & Barrel’s commitment to combining timeless design with digital innovation, and I am eager to contribute to a team that ensures the scalability and security of the company’s enterprise payment technology.\n\nIn my previous role at Cognizant, I designed and maintained six Spring Boot microservices deployed on AWS, supporting over 10,000 users. My work focused heavily on ensuring system stability and security—priorities that are critical for a payments infrastructure. By optimizing API request/response patterns and implementing robust data validation, I improved response times by 25% and reduced runtime errors by 30%. I am also well-versed in Agile methodologies, having collaborated closely with product managers and cross-functional teams to deliver high-quality features within iterative development cycles. These experiences have taught me how to balance technical excellence with the speed required in a modern retail environment.\n\nFurthermore, I have a strong background in software quality and automated testing. I expanded automated test coverage from 65% to 90% using JUnit and Mockito, which significantly reduced regression defects. This focus on reliability is essential for payment systems where accuracy and compliance are paramount. I also have extensive experience with CI/CD concepts and version control, having built automated pipelines with GitHub Actions to streamline deployments. My ability to diagnose and resolve critical production incidents using tools like Splunk has further sharpened my debugging skills and my proactive approach to system maintenance.\n\nDuring my Master's program, I studied Software Testing and Quality Assurance, which allows me to apply rigorous verification standards to every line of code I write. Additionally, my coursework in Advanced Algorithms has equipped me with a strong foundation in data structures, enabling me to design efficient solutions for complex payment workflows. My technical toolkit is well-rounded, spanning Java, JavaScript, and Python, along with SQL and NoSQL database technologies. I am confident that this combination of academic rigor and practical engineering experience makes me a valuable addition to your self-organizing team.\n\nI am enthusiastic about the opportunity to join Crate & Barrel and contribute to the evolution of your payment platforms. I am particularly drawn to this role because of the impact it has on the customer experience and the technical challenge of managing enterprise-scale financial systems. I am confident in my ability to work independently and collaboratively to achieve your sprint goals and deliver exceptional software.\n\nThank you for your time and consideration. I look forward to the possibility of discussing how I can contribute to the growth and success of the Payments team at Crate & Barrel.\n\nSincerely,\nSai Teja Mukkera\nhttps://www.saitejamukkera.dev\nhttps://www.github.com/saitejamukkera	%-------------------------\n% Resume in Latex (ATS Optimized) - 1 Page Jobright Style (Text Only)\n%------------------------\n\n\\documentclass[letterpaper,10pt]{article}\n\n\\usepackage{latexsym}\n\\usepackage[empty]{fullpage}\n\\usepackage{titlesec}\n\\usepackage[usenames,dvipsnames]{color}\n\\usepackage