\textbf{Frontend Technologies:} React, Redux, HTML5, CSS3, Bootstrap, TailwindCSS \\\\\n \\textbf{Databases \\& Cloud:} PostgreSQL, MongoDB, MySQL, AWS (EC2, S3, RDS), Vercel \\\\\n \\textbf{DevOps \\& Tools:} Docker, Git, GitHub Actions, Jenkins, Splunk, Agile/Scrum, JUnit \\\\\n \\textbf{IDEs:} IntelliJ IDEA, VS Code, Cursor, Eclipse, Claude Code\n}}\n\\end{itemize}\n\n\\end{document}	Software Engineer, Payments ApplyLocation: Remote\nWe inspire purpose-filled living that brings beauty and quality to the modern home. Together, we achieve. Associates across our business drive results, innovate, and inspire. Drawn together by our shared values and passion for our customers and our brands, we deliver home furnishings that are expertly designed, responsibly sourced, and bring timeless style and function to people’s homes. From the day we opened our first store in Chicago in 1962 to the digital innovations that engage millions of customers today, our iconic brand is over 60 years in the making—and our story is still unfolding.\n\nWe’re here for it. We think you should be too.\n\nWe are looking for a driven Software Engineer with 2-5 years of experience to contribute to the design, development, and deployment of our software solutions. In this role, you will work on moderately complex projects, contribute to the technical design, and collaborate with a team of talented engineers to deliver high-quality software that meets user needs and business objectives. We are seeking a Developer to join our enterprise payments team and systems. This role will contribute to building our payment technology strategy, ensuring scalability, security, and compliance while delivering exceptional customer experiences.\nThis position is fully remote\n\nThis role is an Individual Contributor\n\n\nA day in the life as a Developer, Payments...\n\nDesign, develop, test, and deploy software features and enhancements with a moderate level of autonomy within an iterative development process\n\nParticipate in agile ceremonies to contribute to effective sprint planning, transparent communication, and the successful delivery of sprint goals\n\nContribute to the technical design of software components and systems\n\nParticipate actively in code reviews, providing and receiving constructive feedback\n\nWork closely with product managers and other cross-functional team members to deeply understand user stories and deliver valuable solutions in alignment with sprint goals\n\nAdhere to and promote agile software development best practices, coding standards, and quality assurance processes\n\nIdentify and resolve software defects and technical issues in a timely manner\n\nContribute to the continuous improvement of development processes and tools through active participation in team retrospectives and feedback loops\n\nEnsure clear and comprehensive documentation of developed features and solutions, contributing to a well-maintained and easily understandable codebase and knowledge base\n\nWhat you’ll bring to the table… \n\nUnderstanding of software development principles, data structures, and algorithms, with an appreciation for agile principles\n\nProficiency in one or more programming languages (e.g., Java, Python, C++, JavaScript, Go)\n\nExperience with software development methodologies (e.g., Agile, Scrum)\n\nProblem-solving, analytical, and debugging skills, with a collaborative approach to finding solutions\n\nCommunication and collaboration skills, with the ability to effectively interact with cross-functional team members\n\nAbility to work independently on assigned tasks and contribute actively as a valued member of a self-organizing team\n\nFamiliarity with software testing frameworks and methodologies\n\nUnderstanding of version control systems (e.g., Git) and CI/CD concepts\n\nBasic knowledge of database technologies (SQL or NoSQL)\n\n\nWe’d love to hear from you if you have…\n\nBachelor's degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering, or a related field (or equivalent practical experience)\n\nMinimum of 2-5 years of professional software development experience\n\nExperience developing and shipping software products or features\n\nExperience working in an agile development environment is a plus\n\n\n#li-remote\n\n\nStarting Rate: $92,000.00 - $130,000.00\nPay ranges will be adjusted upward as needed to comply with applicable state and local law. In addition to your salary, based on your role, associates may be eligible for other compensation including bonuses, sales incentives, and long term incentives.\n\nJob ID R22363\nDate posted 12/24/2025\nPosition Type Full Time\nOur commitment to our associates is of the utmost importance. One of the reasons the company attracts such a diverse group of associates is that we offer a full menu of benefits that are relevant to their lives, both on and off the job. We are proud to offer a comprehensive compensation and benefits package to support eligible part time and full time associates and their families, including:\nMedical/Dental/Vision\nLife insurance and Disability\nRetirement and 401(k) match\nPaid time off, wellness time and volunteer time\nMerchandise discount and EAP resources\nTuition Reimbursement\nMany of these benefits begin on day one, and extend to eligible dependents. To learn more about available benefits please click https://jobs.crateandbarrel.com/benefits\n\nEuromarket Designs, Inc., which does business as Crate & Barrel, Crate & Kids, CB2 and Hudson Grace, will be referred to as “the Company”. The Company is deeply committed to working with and providing reasonable accommodations to individuals with disabilities. If you need a reasonable accommodation for any part of the application process, or in order to perform the essential functions of a position, please contact the location you are applying to here and ask to speak with a manager regarding the nature of your request.\n\nThe Company is an equal opportunity employer; applicants are considered for all positions without regard to race, color, religious creed, sex, national origin, citizenship status, age, physical or mental disability, sexual orientation, gender identity, marital, parental, veteran or military status, unfavorable military discharge, or any other status protected by applicable federal, state or local law.\n\nThe Company participates in E-Verify and will provide the federal government with your Form I-9 information to confirm that you are authorized to work in the US.\n\nState / City Compliance: The Company will consider for employment qualified applicants with criminal history, including arrest and conviction records, in accordance with the Los Angeles Fair Chance Initiative for Hiring and the San Francisco Fair Chance Ordinance.\nJob Applicant Privacy: For details about how the Company collects and uses your personal information, please see our Job Applicant Privacy & Communications Notice.\n\n	R22363	Remote	DRAFT	Software Engineer, Payments	7
21	2026-02-13 13:55:11.8714	Freddie Mac	Sai Teja Mukkera\nWarrensburg, MO\n9139639317\nsaitejamukkera@gmail.com\nhttps://www.linkedin.com/in/saiteja-mukkera\n\nMay 22, 2024\nHiring Manager\nFreddie Mac\nMcLean, VA\n\nRe: Application for Full Stack Software Engineer, Associate II (Job ID: JR16351)\n\nDear Hiring Manager,\nI am writing to express my enthusiastic interest in the Full Stack Software Engineer position within the Loan Closing Advisor (LCLA) and Loan Quality Advisor (LQA) product team at Freddie Mac. Currently pursuing my Master of Science in Computer Science with a 4.0 GPA and holding over two years of professional experience at Cognizant, I am eager to apply my technical curiosity and background in Java and Spring Boot to support Freddie Mac’s mission of Making Home Possible. My experience in building resilient, high-availability software solutions aligns perfectly with your team’s focus on transforming systems into flexible, cloud-native platforms.\n\nDuring my tenure at Cognizant, I specialized in developing scalable microservices using Java and Spring Boot, where I focused on improving operational efficiency and software quality. For instance, I refactored API structures to reduce payload sizes by 40% and implemented strict JSR-303 input validation to ensure data integrity—a critical requirement for underwriting and loan quality applications. I am particularly proud of maintaining a 90% code coverage rate using JUnit and Mockito, which significantly reduced regression defects. This commitment to quality and my experience diagnosing production incidents using Splunk will allow me to contribute immediately to the stability and performance of the LCLA and LQA products.\n\nMy technical foundation is further strengthened by my graduate studies at the University of Central Missouri. During my Master's program, I studied Software Testing and Quality Assurance, which allows me to implement advanced verification strategies that ensure the resilience of mission-critical financial software. Additionally, my coursework in Introduction to Cloud Computing has provided me with a deep understanding of cloud-native architectures, positioning me to help your team transition legacy systems into modern, efficient platforms using tools like Docker, Kubernetes, and OpenShift.\n\nI am highly proficient in Java and Spring Boot for backend development, coupled with hands-on experience in modern front-end technologies like React and TypeScript. I am comfortable working in Agile environments, utilizing Bitbucket and Git for version control, and managing data with both SQL and NoSQL databases like MongoDB. My background in full-stack development, combined with my academic focus on quality assurance and cloud infrastructure, ensures I can deliver high-quality code that meets the rigorous standards of the mortgage technology landscape.\n\nI am genuinely inspired by Freddie Mac’s impact on 90 million families and would welcome the opportunity to bring my technology-first mindset to your team. I am a proactive problem-solver who thrives in fast-paced environments and is committed to continuous learning and customer satisfaction. Thank you for your time and consideration. I look forward to the possibility of discussing how I can contribute to the continued success of the Single-Family IT BTO group.\n\nSincerely,\nSai Teja Mukkera\nhttps://saiteja-dev-portfolio.vercel.app\nhttps://www.github.com/saitejamukkera	%-------------------------\n% Resume in Latex (ATS Optimized) - 1 Page Jobright Style + Icons\n%------------------------\n\n\\documentclass[letterpaper,10pt]{article}\n\n\\usepackage{latexsym}\n\\usepackage[empty]{fullpage}\n\\usepackage{titlesec}\n\\usepackage{marvosym}\n\\usepackage[usenames,dvipsnames]{color}\n\\usepackage{enumitem}\n\\usepackage[hidelinks]{hyperref}\n\\usepackage{fancyhdr}\n\\usepackage{fontawesome5}\n\\usepackage[english]{babel}\n\\usepackage{tabularx}\n\\input{glyphtounicode}\n\n\\pagestyle{fancy}\n\\fancyhf{}\n\\fan