on reliability by expanding the \\textbf{JUnit 5} and \\textbf{Mockito} test suites to \\textbf{90\\% coverage}, identifying critical defects early in the development lifecycle.}\n    \\resumeItem{Proactively resolved \\textbf{40+ production incidents} by analyzing system logs via \\textbf{Splunk}, maintaining platform stability and meeting strict operational service level agreements.}\n    \\resumeItem{Collaborated in an \\textbf{Agile} environment to automate \\textbf{CI/CD} pipelines using \\textbf{GitHub Actions}, leveraging \\textbf{SonarQube} to maintain high code quality standards.}\n  \\resumeItemListEnd\n\n\\resumeSubheading\n  {Associate Software Engineer}{Aug 2021 -- Oct 2022}\n  {Cognizant Technology Solutions}{Hyderabad, India}\n  \\resumeItemListStart\n    \\resumeItem{Contributed to backend feature development using \\textbf{Java} and \\textbf{Spring}, delivering well-documented and modular code for enterprise-scale software solutions.}\n    \\resumeItem{Enhanced system stability by investigating and fixing bugs in \\textbf{RESTful APIs}, utilizing \\textbf{SQL} for data verification and root cause analysis of application defects.}\n    \\resumeItem{Maintained high quality standards by writing comprehensive unit tests with \\textbf{JUnit}, ensuring new code integrated seamlessly with existing legacy components.}\n  \\resumeItemListEnd\n\n\\resumeSubHeadingListEnd\n\n%-----------PROJECTS-----------\n\\section{Projects}\n\\resumeSubHeadingListStart\n\n\\resumeSubheading\n  {Developer Portfolio Website $|$ \\hspace{1pt} \\href{https://saiteja-dev-portfolio.vercel.app} {\\faLink} \\hspace{2pt} \\href{https://github.com/saitejamukkera/Portfolio}{\\faGithub}}{Jan 2025 -- Present}\n  {\\small React, TypeScript, TailwindCSS, Shadcn UI, Framer Motion}{}\n  \\resumeItemListStart\n    \\resumeItem{Architected a responsive SPA using \\textbf{React} and \\textbf{TypeScript}, enforcing strict static typing to minimize runtime errors and enhance codebase scalability.}\n    \\resumeItem{Designed a modular UI system with \\textbf{TailwindCSS} and \\textbf{Shadcn UI}, focusing on \\textbf{component reusability} and dark mode.}\n    \\resumeItem{Optimized frontend performance and SEO strategies, achieving a \\textbf{95+ Google Lighthouse score} across metrics.}\n  \\resumeItemListEnd\n\n\\resumeSubheading\n  {JobRadar (Full-Stack Application) $|$ \\hspace{1pt} \\href{https://job-radar.vercel.app}{\\faLink} \\hspace{2pt} \\href{https://github.com/saitejamukkera/job-portal-fullstack-mern}{\\faGithub}}{Oct 2024 -- Jan 2025}\n  {\\small JavaScript, Node.js, React, MongoDB, Express.js, Redux Toolkit}{}\n  \\resumeItemListStart\n    \\resumeItem{Engineered a scalable Job Board platform using the \\textbf{MERN stack}, implementing \\textbf{RBAC} for Recruiters/Applicants.}\n    \\resumeItem{Developed \\textbf{RESTful APIs} with \\textbf{Express.js} and \\textbf{MongoDB}, enabling advanced filtering and reducing latency by 30\\%.}\n    \\resumeItem{Implemented secure authentication using \\textbf{JWT} and \\textbf{Bcrypt}, managing state with \\textbf{Redux Toolkit}.}\n  \\resumeItemListEnd\n\n\\resumeSubHeadingListEnd\n\n%-----------TECHNICAL SKILLS-----------\n\\section{Technical Skills}\n\\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=0.15in, label={}, itemsep=2pt]\n\\small{\\item{\n \\textbf{Programming Languages}{: Java, SQL, NoSQL (MongoDB), JavaScript, TypeScript, Python} \\\\\n \\textbf{Backend Technologies}{: Spring Boot, Spring, RESTful APIs, Node.js, Express.js} \\\\\n \\textbf{Frontend Technologies}{: React, Redux, HTML5, CSS3, Bootstrap, TailwindCSS} \\\\\n \\textbf{Databases \\& Cloud}{: MongoDB, PostgreSQL, MySQL, AWS (EC2, S3), OpenShift, Docker} \\\\\n \\textbf{DevOps, AI \\& Tools}{: Git, Bitbucket, GitHub Actions, Jenkins, Kubernetes, Splunk, Agile} \\\\\n \\textbf{IDEs}{: IntelliJ IDEA, Eclipse, VS Code, Cursor}\n}}\n\\end{itemize}\n\n\\end{document}	Full Stack Software Engineer, Associate II\nOpened Recently\nLocation  McLean, VACategory  TechnologyJob Id  JR16351\n \nShare via email\nShare via Facebook\nShare via LinkedIn\nShare via twitter\nAt Freddie Mac, our mission of Making Home Possible is what motivates us, and it’s at the core of everything we do. Since our charter in 1970, we have made home possible for more than 90 million families across the country. Join an organization where your work contributes to a greater purpose.\n\nPosition Overview:\nAre you someone who thrives in working in a highly visible, fast paced development environment? Do you have a thorough understanding and passion for excellence in technology and making delivery timelines? If you have proven experience, the drive, and know what it takes to help teams successfully implement fast to market products, we are your next destination employer!\n\nApply to join Freddie Mac’s Loan Closing Advisor (LCLA) and Loan Quality Advisor (LQA) product team as our new Developer. The LQA/LCLA team is an interesting mix of legacy and cloud-based technologies within Single-Family IT’s Business Technology Office (BTO) group.\n\nOur Impact:\nThe SF Underwriting BTO is responsible for technology strategy, delivery and ongoing support for Freddie Mac’s Underwriting applications and services. Our focus is on continuing the mission to transform our systems and processes into resilient, efficient, and flexible platforms by adopting innovative, cloud-native solutions to support industry needs and aligning with our corporate mandates and data strategy!\n\nYour Impact:\nJoining this team means stepping into an Agile environment where you'll collaborate to design, develop, and enhance high quality software solutions that directly support Freddie Mac's core businesses. You'll work closely with project teams and stakeholders to understand user needs, shape system requirements, and create applications that deliver top tier performance, scalability, and efficiency. In this role, you'll not only build new features but also evaluate defects, investigate the causes, and implement smart, timely fixes to keep production systems running smoothly. You'll play a key part in ensuring clear communication around incidents and in optimizing existing applications through well designed enhancements. Alongside the technical challenges, you'll grow through targeted training, mentorship from seasons leader, and opportunities to deepen your understanding of the financial and mortgage technology landscape. You'll refine your analytical leadership, and communication skills, expand your professional network, and even earned sponsorship for valuable technical certifications- all while contributing to impactful, real-world solutions.\n\nQualifications:\nBachelor's degree in Computer Science, Engineering or related discipline; or equivalent experience preferred.\n\nAt least 1-3 years of full-time experience in software development including design, coding, testing, and support\n\nProgramming Languages (Required): Java\n\nQuery Language (Preferred): NoSQL (MongoDB), SQL (RDBMS)\n\nVersioning Control (Preferred): Bitbucket, GIT\n\nFront-end languages (Optional): Angular, HTML, CSS, JavaScript, TypeScript\n\nTools (Preferred): Eclipse, IntelliJ, VSCode\n\nFrameworks (Preferred): Spring, Spring Boot\n\nOther (Preferred): Kubernetes, Docker, OpenShift, MongoDB\n\nMethodologies (Preferred): DevOps, Agile Development\n\nKnowledge of Agile software development project methodologies preferred.\n\nExperience with popular business tools (Windows, Office Professional, Visio, SharePoint, etc.)\n\nDemonstrated analytical ability and problem-solving skills.\n\nExcellent verbal and written communication\n\nOrganized, ability to meet deadlines, self-driven, motivated.\n\nKeys to Success in this Role:\nAbility to work effectively and productively in a team.\n\nTechnology-first mindset, outstanding analytical skills, and drive for innovation\n\nWillingness to try new things, fail fast and learn fast.\n\nWorks under normal supervision. Follows established directions from Team Lead\n\nGood team player\n\nProactive in nature with customer satisfaction as primary goal\n\n	JR16351	McLean, VA	REJECTED	Full Stack Software Engineer, Associate II	7
