estcontainers. My recent work also includes integrating Large Language Models (LLMs) into production-ready applications, aligning with GitHub’s focus on AI-powered developer tools and agentic workflows. I take immense pride in writing maintainable code and taking full ownership of system health, from initial prototype to on-call support.\n\nMy technical foundation is further strengthened by my Master's coursework in Advanced Networking & Security and Software Testing & Quality Assurance. During my Master's program, I studied Advanced Networking & Security, which allows me to contribute to the Identity Core team by implementing sophisticated authentication patterns and ensuring the resilience of GitHub's security infrastructure against modern threats. These academic insights, combined with my professional experience in high-throughput environments, make me well-prepared to handle the planetary scale of GitHub’s systems.\n\nI am a growth-minded engineer who thrives in remote, distributed teams and values a culture of collaboration and diverse thinking. I am particularly excited about the Identity Core team’s mission to provide seamless and secure user experiences. Thank you for your time and consideration. I look forward to the possibility of discussing how I can contribute to the continued success and security of the GitHub platform.\n\nSincerely,\nSai Teja Mukkera\nhttps://www.saitejamukkera.dev\nhttps://www.github.com/saitejamukkera	\\documentclass[a4paper,10pt]{article}\n\n\\usepackage{latexsym}\n\\usepackage[empty]{fullpage}\n\\usepackage{titlesec}\n\\usepackage[usenames,dvipsnames]{color}\n\\usepackage{enumitem}\n\\usepackage[hidelinks]{hyperref}\n\\usepackage{fancyhdr}\n\\usepackage[english]{babel}\n\\usepackage{tabularx}\n\\input{glyphtounicode}\n\n\\pagestyle{fancy}\n\\fancyhf{}\n\\fancyfoot{}\n\\renewcommand{\\headrulewidth}{0pt}\n\\renewcommand{\\footrulewidth}{0pt}\n\n% MARGINS (ATS-safe, 1-page)\n\\addtolength{\\oddsidemargin}{-0.5in}\n\\addtolength{\\eve